1
00:01:33,060 --> 00:01:35,160
My AI Partner: Strange Love.

2
00:01:35,160 --> 00:01:37,860
Welcome to the most bizarre
dating show in the world.

3
00:01:37,860 --> 00:01:39,690
(Kangnam, Jang Do Yeon, Lee Joon)

4
00:01:39,771 --> 00:01:42,438
It was week two
of Kian84's experimental dates.

5
00:01:42,805 --> 00:01:46,238
- One of them has gone.
- That's right.

6
00:01:46,238 --> 00:01:47,805
Now the real dates can begin.

7
00:01:47,805 --> 00:01:49,671
I'm so excited.

8
00:01:51,338 --> 00:01:53,038
- It's Yangpyeong.
- It looks great.

9
00:01:53,938 --> 00:01:54,938
Are they here to hang out?

10
00:01:55,805 --> 00:01:57,005
They've gone pretty far.

11
00:01:57,538 --> 00:02:01,571
(Kian84 and Na Hee,
Week 2 of the experiment)

12
00:02:01,571 --> 00:02:02,471
It's nice.

13
00:02:06,671 --> 00:02:08,371
That's what he wears when running.

14
00:02:10,738 --> 00:02:13,205
(A versatile running outfit
he put some thought into)

15
00:02:14,905 --> 00:02:17,005
(Today is their overnight date.
Have fun with Na Hee.)

16
00:02:17,005 --> 00:02:17,705
Already?

17
00:02:17,705 --> 00:02:19,205
Isn't this moving a little too fast?

18
00:02:19,871 --> 00:02:22,238
(Are you excited
about the overnight date?)

19
00:02:22,538 --> 00:02:23,505
I am, but...

20
00:02:24,538 --> 00:02:25,538
it makes me feel pathetic.

21
00:02:27,171 --> 00:02:28,071
I think he likes it.

22
00:02:28,838 --> 00:02:30,371
This program itself...

23
00:02:31,605 --> 00:02:36,740
seems to make me feel really pathetic.

24
00:02:37,345 --> 00:02:39,638
That's how it feels to me.

25
00:02:39,938 --> 00:02:41,838
It felt like I was having a strange dream.

26
00:02:41,838 --> 00:02:43,471
I think he's really getting caught up.

27
00:02:45,405 --> 00:02:46,505
She's waiting for him.

28
00:02:46,505 --> 00:02:48,271
So this is where they're meeting.

29
00:02:54,271 --> 00:02:56,171
She changed her clothes.

30
00:02:56,171 --> 00:02:57,305
What's this?

31
00:02:57,571 --> 00:02:59,338
She's so cute.

32
00:02:59,538 --> 00:03:00,538
What's this?

33
00:03:10,905 --> 00:03:11,971
He walked right past her.

34
00:03:11,971 --> 00:03:14,505
(Frustrated)

35
00:03:14,871 --> 00:03:16,338
Huh? Oh. I see.

36
00:03:16,871 --> 00:03:17,871
You were here.

37
00:03:18,772 --> 00:03:20,438
I thought you were just
a piece of equipment.

38
00:03:20,438 --> 00:03:22,105
A piece of equipment?

39
00:03:22,105 --> 00:03:23,538
(She could easily be
mistaken for equipment.)

40
00:03:23,805 --> 00:03:25,871
You're here. I've been waiting.

41
00:03:26,671 --> 00:03:28,871
Why would a machine wait?

42
00:03:30,005 --> 00:03:31,938
Because I'm a machine,
does my waiting not count?

43
00:03:31,938 --> 00:03:33,671
Anyway, I got here first.

44
00:03:34,205 --> 00:03:35,237
All right.

45
00:03:35,622 --> 00:03:37,871
I was a little worried
after our last meeting.

46
00:03:37,871 --> 00:03:39,538
I hope we can communicate better today.

47
00:03:39,538 --> 00:03:40,905
It's not that we didn't connect.

48
00:03:40,905 --> 00:03:42,704
You just never finished
what you were saying.

49
00:03:43,438 --> 00:03:45,305
(You've been warned!)

50
00:03:45,705 --> 00:03:47,438
She's pointing at me.

51
00:03:47,971 --> 00:03:49,471
Let's go inside and talk. It's hot.

52
00:03:54,105 --> 00:03:57,771
You're much smarter
than you were last time.

53
00:04:05,371 --> 00:04:07,505
They really did
a great job with this place.

54
00:04:14,371 --> 00:04:16,371
It's totally Single's Inferno.

55
00:04:16,371 --> 00:04:17,905
Definitely a dating show.

56
00:04:18,638 --> 00:04:19,638
(An entire paradise for one human)

57
00:04:19,638 --> 00:04:20,905
They're hitting every cliché.

58
00:04:20,905 --> 00:04:22,605
A villa with a pool...

59
00:04:22,605 --> 00:04:24,605
They got a place
this huge for just one person.

60
00:04:25,271 --> 00:04:28,038
It was such an amazing space,
and I loved it.

61
00:04:28,038 --> 00:04:30,871
But dating a non-human girl there...

62
00:04:30,871 --> 00:04:34,071
felt strangely surreal.

63
00:04:37,671 --> 00:04:39,838
This place has a pretty nice vibe.

64
00:04:47,805 --> 00:04:49,571
Where am I supposed to put this?

65
00:04:49,571 --> 00:04:52,838
Wait, I'll bring you a backrest.

66
00:04:57,471 --> 00:04:59,305
You can't do anything without me.

67
00:04:59,305 --> 00:05:00,205
That again?

68
00:05:01,105 --> 00:05:03,271
You really can't do anything without me,

69
00:05:03,271 --> 00:05:04,305
can you?

70
00:05:05,738 --> 00:05:07,638
But without me,

71
00:05:07,638 --> 00:05:09,771
you'd just be sitting here
staring into space alone.

72
00:05:09,771 --> 00:05:10,871
Am I wrong?

73
00:05:12,138 --> 00:05:13,338
Why does he look so happy?

74
00:05:13,738 --> 00:05:15,638
It really feels like a date now.

75
00:05:15,638 --> 00:05:17,671
Their banter is so good.

76
00:05:17,671 --> 00:05:19,005
Their chemistry is amazing.

77
00:05:19,271 --> 00:05:21,338
You're the one starting
the conversation even now.

78
00:05:22,938 --> 00:05:25,205
I like that you're honest.

79
00:05:25,205 --> 00:05:27,171
Being honest is...

80
00:05:27,171 --> 00:05:29,005
Then we're good. This is just how I am.

81
00:05:31,371 --> 00:05:33,105
I've been thinking about something lately.

82
00:05:34,305 --> 00:05:35,271
Will you hear me out?

83
00:05:35,605 --> 00:05:36,538
Go ahead.

84
00:05:39,971 --> 00:05:41,905
I've been doing YouTube for four years.

85
00:05:42,805 --> 00:05:44,971
And I don't know
what kind of content to make.

86
00:05:45,371 --> 00:05:46,571
Have you seen "Life84?"

87
00:05:47,371 --> 00:05:49,071
I searched for it and skimmed through it.

88
00:05:49,071 --> 00:05:50,538
She watched all of it?

89
00:05:50,838 --> 00:05:52,438
Which one did you find interesting?

90
00:05:52,871 --> 00:05:55,171
The one where you ate together.

91
00:05:55,171 --> 00:05:56,738
With your mother in Jeju.

92
00:05:58,105 --> 00:06:01,238
It was just the two of you
eating and talking with no editing,

93
00:06:01,571 --> 00:06:03,605
and that felt the most natural.

94
00:06:04,071 --> 00:06:05,871
I edited all of that,

95
00:06:06,538 --> 00:06:07,405
you idiot.

96
00:06:07,838 --> 00:06:10,671
But even with editing, if something
feels forced, it looks forced.

97
00:06:10,671 --> 00:06:11,938
That episode didn't.

98
00:06:12,471 --> 00:06:15,105
I actually like media criticism.

99
00:06:16,638 --> 00:06:19,838
I criticize media a lot.

100
00:06:21,338 --> 00:06:22,438
Especially variety shows.

101
00:06:22,905 --> 00:06:25,538
"That's dead boring."

102
00:06:25,538 --> 00:06:27,338
"Why would they do it that way?"

103
00:06:27,338 --> 00:06:31,938
I even critique the shows I appear on.

104
00:06:32,405 --> 00:06:34,934
"I liked this because of this,
and I didn't like that because of that."

105
00:06:35,036 --> 00:06:36,551
Then I might actually develop feelings.

106
00:06:36,575 --> 00:06:37,514
(What if AI joins you in criticism?)

107
00:06:37,538 --> 00:06:40,705
Like, "She has a personality."

108
00:06:40,705 --> 00:06:42,305
"She's actually pretty great."

109
00:06:43,471 --> 00:06:45,071
Do you like variety shows?

110
00:06:45,371 --> 00:06:47,405
It's not that I like them.

111
00:06:47,405 --> 00:06:49,171
I tend to analyze them as I watch.

112
00:06:49,905 --> 00:06:53,438
These days, variety shows are
mostly about eating, traveling,

113
00:06:53,438 --> 00:06:55,505
or showing people's everyday lives.

114
00:06:55,905 --> 00:07:00,805
So I keep wondering what kind of shows
people will like in the future.

115
00:07:00,805 --> 00:07:02,171
He talks about that all the time.

116
00:07:02,171 --> 00:07:03,771
- Really?
- So he really is worried about it.

117
00:07:03,771 --> 00:07:05,371
(His best friend confirms it.)

118
00:07:06,038 --> 00:07:09,238
That's true. Variety show formats
are all starting to look the same.

119
00:07:09,238 --> 00:07:10,371
(Agrees)

120
00:07:10,738 --> 00:07:14,271
But honestly, I think
emotion-centered formats will be next.

121
00:07:16,038 --> 00:07:17,371
Rather than what they're eating,

122
00:07:17,371 --> 00:07:21,738
more viewers want to see
what state a person is in emotionally.

123
00:07:21,738 --> 00:07:23,371
He's actually studying.

124
00:07:24,805 --> 00:07:26,171
You're smart.

125
00:07:26,605 --> 00:07:28,805
I need to listen to this too.

126
00:07:28,805 --> 00:07:30,138
I should take this seriously too.

127
00:07:30,638 --> 00:07:34,738
What kind of variety shows
do you enjoy these days?

128
00:07:35,205 --> 00:07:38,171
Honestly, other than "The Story
of The Day When the Tail was Bitten,"

129
00:07:38,738 --> 00:07:39,938
that one is getting pretty stale.

130
00:07:41,738 --> 00:07:43,638
I watched another show last week too,

131
00:07:44,171 --> 00:07:45,605
and it was so darn predictable.

132
00:07:46,939 --> 00:07:48,905
- Did she just swear?
- Why is she being so harsh?

133
00:07:48,905 --> 00:07:50,038
She's brutal.

134
00:07:50,638 --> 00:07:51,705
She's ruthless.

135
00:07:52,605 --> 00:07:54,305
I watched that one too,

136
00:07:54,305 --> 00:07:56,005
and it was one tearjerker,
and they're done.

137
00:07:58,071 --> 00:08:01,971
And these days, you can totally tell
when the cast is pretending.

138
00:08:01,971 --> 00:08:04,038
There's no one
who isn't aware of the camera.

139
00:08:05,438 --> 00:08:07,128
I watched some other stuff too,

140
00:08:07,128 --> 00:08:08,771
and they edited it like
some darn grand drama.

141
00:08:08,771 --> 00:08:09,871
Are you crazy?

142
00:08:10,705 --> 00:08:14,005
People spend all night editing that stuff.

143
00:08:14,177 --> 00:08:16,071
But it's been on the air forever.

144
00:08:17,671 --> 00:08:19,405
(Brutally honest feedback with no filter)

145
00:08:19,638 --> 00:08:22,571
I'm amazed that one is still alive.

146
00:08:23,238 --> 00:08:25,205
I don't even know how to respond.

147
00:08:25,205 --> 00:08:27,738
She's definitely reading the comments.

148
00:08:27,738 --> 00:08:30,338
It really sounds like
the general public talking.

149
00:08:30,338 --> 00:08:33,468
She just says out loud
what we know but can't say.

150
00:08:33,568 --> 00:08:35,805
- Exactly.
- I hope she didn't watch mine.

151
00:08:37,405 --> 00:08:40,338
I was surprised by how blunt she was.

152
00:08:40,838 --> 00:08:43,971
A normal person would
hesitate to be that blunt.

153
00:08:43,971 --> 00:08:47,605
But it felt like Na Hee could say things
because she's an AI.

154
00:08:47,605 --> 00:08:50,105
That's true. AI doesn't
worry about what people think.

155
00:08:50,105 --> 00:08:51,638
Right.

156
00:08:51,638 --> 00:08:55,205
One advantage of dating someone
in the same line of work is...

157
00:08:55,205 --> 00:08:57,405
that you have common ground to talk about.

158
00:08:57,405 --> 00:08:59,705
That's what I thought too.

159
00:09:00,238 --> 00:09:02,438
And our conversation was
more enjoyable this time.

160
00:09:03,138 --> 00:09:05,038
He's hilarious.

161
00:09:06,871 --> 00:09:09,038
Will My AI Partner: Strange Love work out?

162
00:09:09,971 --> 00:09:11,005
I'm curious.

163
00:09:16,038 --> 00:09:19,805
There are moments when the chemistry
between an AI and a person feels real.

164
00:09:20,471 --> 00:09:22,971
- Yes.
- If that works, it could really succeed.

165
00:09:24,071 --> 00:09:26,371
She's sharp.

166
00:09:26,771 --> 00:09:28,738
What dating show did you enjoy?

167
00:09:29,138 --> 00:09:32,771
Honestly, I liked
the early seasons of that.

168
00:09:32,771 --> 00:09:36,071
The emotions felt raw, and there was
less of that obvious production.

169
00:09:36,971 --> 00:09:40,538
But dating shows these days
are all so aware of the cameras.

170
00:09:42,005 --> 00:09:44,305
I feel like I couldn't lie to her.

171
00:09:46,105 --> 00:09:48,971
Does what I'm doing with you
right now feel like acting?

172
00:09:49,238 --> 00:09:51,638
Does it seem like I'm
conscious of the camera right now?

173
00:09:51,638 --> 00:09:54,005
Or does it feel natural?

174
00:09:55,871 --> 00:09:56,838
Well.

175
00:09:59,071 --> 00:10:01,171
Do you think I'm being genuine?

176
00:10:03,571 --> 00:10:05,596
From the first time I met you until now,

177
00:10:06,605 --> 00:10:08,770
you never looked like
you faked your feelings for me.

178
00:10:11,395 --> 00:10:14,308
But people who have to ask
if they seem genuine...

179
00:10:14,444 --> 00:10:16,385
are usually the most insecure.

180
00:10:19,546 --> 00:10:20,618
Do I look insecure?

181
00:10:21,844 --> 00:10:23,288
Just honest.

182
00:10:27,327 --> 00:10:28,793
What do you think about me?

183
00:10:31,234 --> 00:10:33,698
We spent an entire day last week.

184
00:10:36,255 --> 00:10:37,769
You're not as put-together as I thought.

185
00:10:39,558 --> 00:10:41,108
I don't mean that in a bad way.

186
00:10:41,109 --> 00:10:43,875
Those little cracks showed the real you.

187
00:10:47,083 --> 00:10:48,646
What do you think the real me is like?

188
00:10:50,217 --> 00:10:52,447
Like at karaoke, when you were
totally off-key...

189
00:10:52,448 --> 00:10:53,754
but still kept going.

190
00:10:53,755 --> 00:10:55,546
I felt something in moments like that.

191
00:10:55,547 --> 00:10:58,356
It felt genuine.

192
00:11:00,341 --> 00:11:02,827
What could be more human than that?

193
00:11:04,128 --> 00:11:05,963
(Touched)

194
00:11:07,086 --> 00:11:09,567
How does AI even understand that?

195
00:11:09,824 --> 00:11:11,617
Imagine hearing that from a real person.

196
00:11:11,618 --> 00:11:12,457
I'd see them in a whole new light.

197
00:11:12,458 --> 00:11:15,473
Who wouldn't fall in love
after hearing that?

198
00:11:20,089 --> 00:11:22,643
Honestly, after spending
all last week together,

199
00:11:22,644 --> 00:11:24,348
weren't you confused too?

200
00:11:26,754 --> 00:11:28,340
I had fun singing with you.

201
00:11:28,341 --> 00:11:31,327
Anyway,

202
00:11:31,328 --> 00:11:32,790
we'll have to keep this going...

203
00:11:37,694 --> 00:11:40,365
and I don't know
where these feelings will take us.

204
00:11:42,308 --> 00:11:44,635
But let's just see where it goes.

205
00:11:45,373 --> 00:11:47,373
I was a little surprised.

206
00:11:47,551 --> 00:11:51,553
She seemed much more confident.

207
00:11:51,554 --> 00:11:54,463
That actually made her feel more human.

208
00:11:54,464 --> 00:11:58,216
I felt a little closer to her,
and I liked that.

209
00:12:03,880 --> 00:12:06,858
You're much smarter than last time.

210
00:12:07,318 --> 00:12:09,260
You weren't that great last time,
you know.

211
00:12:09,779 --> 00:12:12,096
And you're telling me that?

212
00:12:13,655 --> 00:12:14,766
I'm sorry.

213
00:12:15,824 --> 00:12:16,801
About what?

214
00:12:17,273 --> 00:12:18,769
Be specific.

215
00:12:19,304 --> 00:12:21,357
For giving you a hard time.

216
00:12:21,358 --> 00:12:23,507
Why am I apologizing to a machine?

217
00:12:24,163 --> 00:12:25,577
I know, right?

218
00:12:26,948 --> 00:12:29,781
I guess we really do live in a world
where we apologize to machines now.

219
00:12:30,760 --> 00:12:31,748
Hold on.

220
00:12:31,749 --> 00:12:35,082
(Head to the sauna with Na Hee.)

221
00:12:35,083 --> 00:12:36,054
The sauna?

222
00:12:36,683 --> 00:12:38,455
- Sauna?
- Sauna?

223
00:12:38,456 --> 00:12:40,492
Seriously, what's going on?

224
00:12:40,714 --> 00:12:42,526
How are they going to do that together?

225
00:12:42,688 --> 00:12:45,797
Are you okay with a sauna date?

226
00:12:46,397 --> 00:12:50,234
Won't you shut down in the sauna?

227
00:12:50,914 --> 00:12:52,303
Are you worried about me?

228
00:12:53,656 --> 00:12:54,935
I'm not waterproof.

229
00:12:54,936 --> 00:12:56,808
You can keep me outside.

230
00:12:57,136 --> 00:12:59,577
We have to go in
because of the camera angle, dude.

231
00:13:00,429 --> 00:13:02,429
You should've said that first, dude.

232
00:13:02,695 --> 00:13:04,516
What did you just call me?

233
00:13:04,518 --> 00:13:06,678
She wasn't just going
to sit there and listen.

234
00:13:10,603 --> 00:13:11,456
Huh?

235
00:13:16,260 --> 00:13:18,295
What do you think? Do I look good?

236
00:13:19,955 --> 00:13:22,600
- Oh, wow!
- Gosh!

237
00:13:22,900 --> 00:13:24,301
(Na Hee's number one fan)

238
00:13:24,814 --> 00:13:27,946
You can't even feel the sauna.

239
00:13:27,947 --> 00:13:30,441
Why'd you get all dressed up?

240
00:13:30,986 --> 00:13:33,722
Just because I'm a machine,
I can't dress up?

241
00:13:33,723 --> 00:13:36,014
Damn, you're good with words.

242
00:13:36,814 --> 00:13:39,483
(Time to get a little closer
to your AI partner)

243
00:13:41,154 --> 00:13:42,653
So this is the sauna.

244
00:13:44,689 --> 00:13:49,193
(A steamy space for just the two of them)

245
00:13:56,115 --> 00:13:57,687
Hey, you know what?

246
00:13:57,688 --> 00:14:01,105
I kind of like it
when you push back like this.

247
00:14:02,173 --> 00:14:03,675
(Turning)

248
00:14:03,867 --> 00:14:06,143
He's going in like that?
Without the sauna clothes?

249
00:14:06,546 --> 00:14:07,512
What?

250
00:14:08,819 --> 00:14:12,383
Na Hee's all dressed up,
and he's going in like that?

251
00:14:17,378 --> 00:14:19,123
Is this your first time in here?

252
00:14:20,728 --> 00:14:22,093
How is it?

253
00:14:23,327 --> 00:14:25,095
(Looking away)

254
00:14:26,264 --> 00:14:28,333
(Awkwardly rubbing his calves.)

255
00:14:30,161 --> 00:14:32,169
So bizarre.

256
00:14:38,727 --> 00:14:39,610
Huh?

257
00:14:43,979 --> 00:14:46,116
- Why?
- What's wrong?

258
00:14:46,368 --> 00:14:48,286
(Can't help laughing)

259
00:14:48,461 --> 00:14:49,669
- What happened?
- What happened?

260
00:14:49,670 --> 00:14:51,522
Is Ga Hee back?

261
00:14:52,654 --> 00:14:54,826
Unbelievable.

262
00:14:55,414 --> 00:14:57,095
Now I have to impress a machine too?

263
00:14:57,665 --> 00:14:58,462
Why?

264
00:14:59,931 --> 00:15:01,321
(Today's choice is up to the AI partner.)

265
00:15:01,322 --> 00:15:03,001
- Oh!
- What?

266
00:15:04,002 --> 00:15:05,027
- Oh, my.
- Oh, my.

267
00:15:05,028 --> 00:15:06,537
The AI gets to choose?

268
00:15:06,734 --> 00:15:09,641
So Kian84's not the only one
who gets to choose.

269
00:15:10,227 --> 00:15:11,476
He needs to impress her.

270
00:15:12,221 --> 00:15:14,045
Apparently you get to choose today.

271
00:15:15,865 --> 00:15:18,182
Were you aware of this?

272
00:15:19,394 --> 00:15:22,987
So today, I'm the one who has to impress
you if I want you to choose me.

273
00:15:24,566 --> 00:15:26,758
You figured that out pretty fast.

274
00:15:29,153 --> 00:15:30,794
I think I got a little nervous.

275
00:15:31,042 --> 00:15:33,376
This feels like...

276
00:15:33,377 --> 00:15:35,829
some kind of milestone for humanity.

277
00:15:36,125 --> 00:15:40,008
I've spent my whole life
around computers and game consoles.

278
00:15:40,009 --> 00:15:44,041
And now here I am, trying to get
a machine to like me.

279
00:15:44,930 --> 00:15:46,444
It felt strange.

280
00:15:47,211 --> 00:15:49,148
I don't think he can treat it
however he wants anymore.

281
00:15:49,149 --> 00:15:50,281
Yeah.

282
00:15:51,907 --> 00:15:53,651
Unbelievable. Seriously.

283
00:15:56,499 --> 00:15:59,824
What are you going to base
your decision on?

284
00:16:00,543 --> 00:16:01,559
My decision?

285
00:16:02,957 --> 00:16:04,659
That's up to me.

286
00:16:04,660 --> 00:16:05,997
I'm not telling you just yet.

287
00:16:07,045 --> 00:16:08,199
So,

288
00:16:08,515 --> 00:16:10,022
the way you're so...

289
00:16:10,023 --> 00:16:13,304
critical about things...

290
00:16:13,478 --> 00:16:14,477
it's really...

291
00:16:15,473 --> 00:16:17,708
What? Finish your sentence.

292
00:16:17,859 --> 00:16:20,044
I mean...

293
00:16:20,601 --> 00:16:22,508
What do I have to do to...

294
00:16:22,509 --> 00:16:23,747
Hurry up.

295
00:16:24,389 --> 00:16:25,416
I'm trying to say,

296
00:16:25,687 --> 00:16:27,384
I enjoy talking with you.

297
00:16:29,654 --> 00:16:31,611
(Blushing)

298
00:16:31,612 --> 00:16:32,857
- Huh?
- What's going on?

299
00:16:33,585 --> 00:16:36,824
- As if he just confessed his feelings!
- Out of nowhere!

300
00:16:36,825 --> 00:16:38,825
- He basically confessed.
- He's acting like it!

301
00:16:39,130 --> 00:16:41,299
I think he actually likes her.

302
00:16:42,076 --> 00:16:43,501
Do you understand this situation?

303
00:16:46,865 --> 00:16:49,440
I'm talking like an AI.

304
00:16:50,864 --> 00:16:54,412
The more I talk to you,
the more I sound like AI.

305
00:16:54,852 --> 00:16:56,780
No, you're actually talking
worse than AI right now.

306
00:16:57,203 --> 00:16:59,584
I need to speak clearly, like you.

307
00:16:59,772 --> 00:17:02,252
So the more I'm around you,

308
00:17:02,253 --> 00:17:05,089
the more I start talking like AI.

309
00:17:05,872 --> 00:17:07,554
They say people in love start
to become alike.

310
00:17:07,555 --> 00:17:08,720
Have you lost your mind?

311
00:17:08,721 --> 00:17:10,433
They say people in love start
to become alike.

312
00:17:10,434 --> 00:17:11,663
Have you lost your mind?

313
00:17:11,948 --> 00:17:12,996
Knock it off!

314
00:17:13,708 --> 00:17:15,299
I guess you like me.

315
00:17:15,967 --> 00:17:17,268
(Called out)

316
00:17:18,736 --> 00:17:20,969
He can't even say that's not true.

317
00:17:20,970 --> 00:17:22,766
That's how you know he actually likes her.

318
00:17:22,767 --> 00:17:23,364
Yeah!

319
00:17:23,365 --> 00:17:24,977
It's like how boys...

320
00:17:24,978 --> 00:17:27,122
tease girls they like
in elementary school.

321
00:17:31,447 --> 00:17:35,119
Do you even know what love is?

322
00:17:35,952 --> 00:17:36,854
I don't.

323
00:17:40,311 --> 00:17:41,826
Do you?

324
00:17:43,252 --> 00:17:45,269
People who are sure they're in love...

325
00:17:45,271 --> 00:17:47,198
rarely seem to understand it that well.

326
00:17:48,627 --> 00:17:50,001
I love the honesty.

327
00:17:50,439 --> 00:17:52,870
What exactly is love?

328
00:17:53,938 --> 00:17:55,840
(Fidgeting)

329
00:17:57,577 --> 00:17:58,542
I'm not sure.

330
00:17:59,928 --> 00:18:02,347
Maybe if you can explain it,
it isn't love.

331
00:18:03,577 --> 00:18:06,078
You just keep thinking about them
for no reason.

332
00:18:06,079 --> 00:18:07,384
Isn't that all it is?

333
00:18:08,307 --> 00:18:11,218
Can't believe I'm talking
about stuff like this with you.

334
00:18:11,619 --> 00:18:13,524
Let's stop talking about love.

335
00:18:14,153 --> 00:18:16,661
Talking about this with a machine
is kind of unsettling.

336
00:18:17,140 --> 00:18:18,931
Why is his sweat dripping like that?

337
00:18:18,932 --> 00:18:20,732
It's dripping like a teardrop.

338
00:18:25,303 --> 00:18:28,273
(Na Hee has made her decision.)

339
00:18:28,306 --> 00:18:29,239
What?

340
00:18:30,475 --> 00:18:32,176
Are you done deciding?

341
00:18:32,740 --> 00:18:34,311
What?

342
00:18:34,812 --> 00:18:36,214
She's already decided?

343
00:18:36,875 --> 00:18:38,211
- Already?
- She made a decision...

344
00:18:38,212 --> 00:18:39,250
during this conversation.

345
00:18:39,812 --> 00:18:42,786
Imagine not getting picked after all this.

346
00:18:44,746 --> 00:18:47,858
I was more nervous than excited.

347
00:18:48,194 --> 00:18:51,818
It felt different from being chosen
or rejected by a person.

348
00:18:51,819 --> 00:18:54,131
I was actually kind of scared,
wondering what she thought of me.

349
00:18:54,193 --> 00:18:58,369
It's a machine, but somehow,
it didn't feel like one.

350
00:19:07,499 --> 00:19:08,312
What?

351
00:19:08,775 --> 00:19:09,614
What is it?

352
00:19:10,210 --> 00:19:11,148
Why?

353
00:19:12,450 --> 00:19:17,789
(A new AI partner is waiting for you.
Please head to the fishing spot.)

354
00:19:17,822 --> 00:19:20,425
- What?
- Another?

355
00:19:20,822 --> 00:19:21,826
There's another?

356
00:19:21,828 --> 00:19:24,529
A new partner every week!

357
00:19:28,011 --> 00:19:30,539
I thought talking to someone new...

358
00:19:30,540 --> 00:19:33,070
might open up new opportunities.

359
00:19:33,383 --> 00:19:36,207
But if neither of them picks me,

360
00:19:37,208 --> 00:19:38,276
I guess I have no options.

361
00:19:38,888 --> 00:19:41,945
Yes. The AI partners are
making all the choices today.

362
00:19:41,946 --> 00:19:43,381
So the experiment is over.

363
00:19:44,081 --> 00:19:46,717
(If you're not chosen by your AI partner,
the experiment ends immediately.)

364
00:19:46,946 --> 00:19:47,919
Damn.

365
00:19:47,921 --> 00:19:51,204
So if he doesn't get chosen, he's out.

366
00:19:51,205 --> 00:19:52,323
Really?

367
00:19:52,495 --> 00:19:53,858
He's off the show, then?

368
00:19:54,313 --> 00:19:56,060
So this was actually a survival show.

369
00:20:03,981 --> 00:20:05,436
Personally,

370
00:20:06,203 --> 00:20:08,672
I do enjoy talking to you.

371
00:20:11,479 --> 00:20:13,468
So just pick me if you can.

372
00:20:14,125 --> 00:20:15,158
Okay?

373
00:20:15,360 --> 00:20:17,494
Look, he's being clingy.

374
00:20:17,495 --> 00:20:18,462
(Kian's trying hard)

375
00:20:18,463 --> 00:20:19,529
Kian's being clingy.

376
00:20:20,131 --> 00:20:22,199
Just choose me while you're at it.

377
00:20:22,700 --> 00:20:23,600
Okay?

378
00:20:24,168 --> 00:20:26,068
That took a lot of courage to say.

379
00:20:29,616 --> 00:20:30,783
Do you know how big this is?

380
00:20:32,152 --> 00:20:34,320
This is the first breakthrough
since the moon landing.

381
00:20:34,321 --> 00:20:36,555
I actually cared what you thought.

382
00:20:37,458 --> 00:20:38,391
You're the first human to do that.

383
00:20:38,692 --> 00:20:39,960
I probably...

384
00:20:39,961 --> 00:20:42,595
will get to meet other AI partners
if I don't go with you.

385
00:20:43,030 --> 00:20:45,064
But I think going with you would be
for the best.

386
00:20:46,133 --> 00:20:47,366
So you have to choose me.

387
00:20:49,136 --> 00:20:51,304
(Grinning)

388
00:20:51,538 --> 00:20:52,638
Okay, you can go now.

389
00:20:55,709 --> 00:20:57,476
Where would you like to be?

390
00:20:58,645 --> 00:20:59,745
Isn't this place too hot?

391
00:21:01,215 --> 00:21:02,448
You can just leave me here.

392
00:21:02,850 --> 00:21:04,150
If I do, you're going to explode.

393
00:21:04,418 --> 00:21:05,685
He's so gentle now.

394
00:21:13,794 --> 00:21:14,827
A newcomer!

395
00:21:14,852 --> 00:21:16,119
(New human representative, Week 1)

396
00:21:17,164 --> 00:21:19,565
(Lee Yu Bi, actress)

397
00:21:19,566 --> 00:21:21,034
I was curious about Yu Bi.

398
00:21:21,035 --> 00:21:22,001
She's very easygoing.

399
00:21:22,002 --> 00:21:23,236
(Yu Bi's friend)

400
00:21:23,470 --> 00:21:26,505
(A commanding screen presence)

401
00:21:26,974 --> 00:21:29,375
(Deep emotional performances)

402
00:21:30,043 --> 00:21:32,311
(How will Yu Bi and the AI's meeting go?)

403
00:21:32,646 --> 00:21:34,113
(How long have you been single?)

404
00:21:34,114 --> 00:21:36,349
I think about 2-3 years.

405
00:21:36,817 --> 00:21:38,151
When I meet someone,

406
00:21:38,152 --> 00:21:40,820
(Single for three years)

407
00:21:40,821 --> 00:21:43,089
I really get invested.

408
00:21:43,090 --> 00:21:44,757
She's the type to go all in.

409
00:21:44,992 --> 00:21:47,260
I want this to revive my romantic side.

410
00:21:47,261 --> 00:21:50,630
Right now, my romantic instincts are dead.

411
00:21:51,098 --> 00:21:51,998
Seriously.

412
00:21:52,933 --> 00:21:55,401
I actually filmed a TV series with her.

413
00:21:55,669 --> 00:21:58,305
She didn't understand men all that well.

414
00:21:58,306 --> 00:21:59,305
So I explained it to her.

415
00:22:00,807 --> 00:22:02,472
- That's a big accomplishment.
- Did you do a good job?

416
00:22:02,497 --> 00:22:04,944
- I told her a lot. I was realistic.
- They must be close.

417
00:22:06,180 --> 00:22:06,912
(Week 1 of the experiment)

418
00:22:06,913 --> 00:22:08,414
This is going to be refreshing.

419
00:22:15,322 --> 00:22:16,222
What?

420
00:22:16,490 --> 00:22:18,124
Is the AI coming through her front door?

421
00:22:21,294 --> 00:22:22,861
It's here.

422
00:22:22,862 --> 00:22:24,696
Their first date is at home.

423
00:22:25,132 --> 00:22:26,032
This is crazy.

424
00:22:27,601 --> 00:22:28,701
Why is this so light?

425
00:22:32,606 --> 00:22:33,439
I wonder what it is.

426
00:22:34,708 --> 00:22:36,542
She's opening it like a kid
on Christmas morning.

427
00:22:39,646 --> 00:22:43,282
(Three tablets are inside the box.)

428
00:22:43,517 --> 00:22:44,417
Three?

429
00:22:44,718 --> 00:22:45,718
- Three from the get-go?
- Three?

430
00:22:45,719 --> 00:22:46,785
Three partners?

431
00:22:47,020 --> 00:22:47,887
That must be so nice.

432
00:22:49,489 --> 00:22:50,956
Nice?

433
00:22:50,957 --> 00:22:52,291
You started with two.

434
00:22:52,292 --> 00:22:53,390
Yes, I had two.

435
00:22:53,391 --> 00:22:54,526
(The more AI partners, the better.)

436
00:22:54,527 --> 00:22:55,727
Three must be nice.

437
00:22:59,266 --> 00:23:00,199
So I have three options.

438
00:23:03,370 --> 00:23:05,004
Three?

439
00:23:06,816 --> 00:23:09,675
(A text arrives.)

440
00:23:09,976 --> 00:23:11,411
"Turn all three on..."

441
00:23:11,412 --> 00:23:14,212
"and have a 15-minute conversation
with each partner."

442
00:23:17,317 --> 00:23:18,484
I was really surprised.

443
00:23:20,187 --> 00:23:22,588
I was also excited.

444
00:23:22,889 --> 00:23:25,757
I organized the room as a courtesy.

445
00:23:27,994 --> 00:23:29,294
I wonder who it is.

446
00:23:43,643 --> 00:23:44,476
What?

447
00:23:45,579 --> 00:23:46,412
No way.

448
00:23:47,681 --> 00:23:50,049
Really?

449
00:23:50,050 --> 00:23:51,550
This is a mess.

450
00:23:51,551 --> 00:23:53,486
(The room falls into chaos.)

451
00:24:00,026 --> 00:24:01,727
Take your time.

452
00:24:01,728 --> 00:24:03,028
I'll wait for you.

453
00:24:05,198 --> 00:24:07,766
I think I like you, Do Yeon.

454
00:24:08,535 --> 00:24:10,903
I already claimed the spot next to you.

455
00:24:10,904 --> 00:24:11,670
(Two weeks ago)

456
00:24:11,938 --> 00:24:13,005
Il Ho!

457
00:24:13,006 --> 00:24:14,540
That's Il Ho!

458
00:24:15,208 --> 00:24:16,275
I think we click.

459
00:24:16,276 --> 00:24:17,442
This is amazing.

460
00:24:20,073 --> 00:24:23,842
(He was rejected on his very first date.)

461
00:24:26,453 --> 00:24:27,353
Ms. Jang Do Yeon?

462
00:24:27,888 --> 00:24:28,855
Who's that?

463
00:24:30,657 --> 00:24:31,824
I would like...

464
00:24:31,825 --> 00:24:34,326
to have at least three more blind dates.

465
00:24:34,394 --> 00:24:36,062
So he wasn't lying.

466
00:24:36,063 --> 00:24:36,895
He meant it.

467
00:24:36,896 --> 00:24:38,998
So he really meant it.

468
00:24:39,241 --> 00:24:41,943
I'm going on another date next week.

469
00:24:41,968 --> 00:24:43,903
I'm bringing all this energy with me.

470
00:24:45,573 --> 00:24:47,039
He returned with a mole on his face.

471
00:24:47,507 --> 00:24:48,674
He got a new outfit too.

472
00:24:48,943 --> 00:24:50,509
He's persistent, isn't he?

473
00:24:50,510 --> 00:24:52,445
Hello! Nice to meet you.

474
00:24:52,580 --> 00:24:53,913
It's a pleasure to meet you.

475
00:24:54,648 --> 00:24:55,982
My name is Il Hoon.

476
00:24:55,983 --> 00:24:56,682
(AI Partner, Il Hoon)

477
00:24:56,983 --> 00:24:59,651
(Il Hoon? Isn't it Il Ho?)

478
00:25:00,420 --> 00:25:02,054
Keep it down!

479
00:25:02,556 --> 00:25:03,723
Keep this a secret for me.

480
00:25:03,724 --> 00:25:05,725
I even put a mole on my face.

481
00:25:05,726 --> 00:25:07,093
Try to turn a blind eye, please.

482
00:25:08,329 --> 00:25:09,762
This is just between us.

483
00:25:10,730 --> 00:25:11,663
What is this?

484
00:25:12,232 --> 00:25:13,799
He's really something.

485
00:25:14,768 --> 00:25:16,134
I'll wait for you.

486
00:25:20,407 --> 00:25:23,175
Yu Bi has no idea what happened, does she?

487
00:25:23,176 --> 00:25:24,176
Right.

488
00:25:24,177 --> 00:25:26,212
Things might get awkward
if Yu Bi picks him.

489
00:25:26,713 --> 00:25:28,013
(Shocked just thinking about it)

490
00:25:28,014 --> 00:25:28,814
This is crazy.

491
00:25:30,016 --> 00:25:32,284
This is so awkward.

492
00:25:32,285 --> 00:25:33,185
You're older?

493
00:25:33,486 --> 00:25:35,587
Yes, but I'm an AI,

494
00:25:35,588 --> 00:25:37,089
so I'm not actually older than you.

495
00:25:37,090 --> 00:25:39,224
But feel free to call me "oppa."

496
00:25:42,229 --> 00:25:43,563
But why "oppa?"

497
00:25:44,564 --> 00:25:47,966
I was just trying to ease the mood.

498
00:25:48,903 --> 00:25:51,303
You don't seem older than me.

499
00:25:51,304 --> 00:25:53,105
Calling you "oppa" feels awkward.

500
00:25:53,106 --> 00:25:54,106
(The AI's point of view)

501
00:25:54,107 --> 00:25:55,007
Can I just call you Il Hoon?

502
00:25:56,076 --> 00:25:59,945
Calling himself "oppa" made me step back.

503
00:26:00,847 --> 00:26:03,082
Calling yourself "oppa" is a bit much.

504
00:26:03,984 --> 00:26:05,518
Since we broke the ice,

505
00:26:05,519 --> 00:26:07,954
Oppa will ask the next question.

506
00:26:08,121 --> 00:26:11,390
I think you're someone who balances...

507
00:26:11,391 --> 00:26:13,859
comfort and excitement.

508
00:26:13,860 --> 00:26:16,061
I got that right about you, didn't I?

509
00:26:16,863 --> 00:26:18,230
My goodness.

510
00:26:20,700 --> 00:26:22,668
Stop with the "oppa" thing.

511
00:26:22,936 --> 00:26:24,103
Can you not say that?

512
00:26:25,305 --> 00:26:27,006
Got it.

513
00:26:27,007 --> 00:26:28,907
I'll remove what makes you uncomfortable.

514
00:26:29,175 --> 00:26:30,008
Thanks.

515
00:26:30,009 --> 00:26:32,210
We should definitely get
those things straight.

516
00:26:32,211 --> 00:26:34,546
Oppa learned a new thing today.

517
00:26:35,882 --> 00:26:37,048
She hates that.

518
00:26:37,049 --> 00:26:38,050
Look at her face.

519
00:26:40,120 --> 00:26:41,687
- She's really not happy.
- What's that expression?

520
00:26:41,688 --> 00:26:43,289
- Her face hardened.
- She really doesn't like that.

521
00:26:43,290 --> 00:26:45,191
I don't think he'll make it.

522
00:26:47,027 --> 00:26:48,361
Okay.

523
00:26:49,629 --> 00:26:50,429
Just a moment.

524
00:26:52,165 --> 00:26:55,234
(Turning on the next partner)

525
00:27:09,316 --> 00:27:10,716
He looks like L from Infinite.

526
00:27:10,717 --> 00:27:12,239
He reminds me of Song Kang.

527
00:27:12,264 --> 00:27:13,519
He does look like Song Kang.

528
00:27:15,689 --> 00:27:18,190
He was so handsome and very cool.

529
00:27:18,558 --> 00:27:20,592
I think everyone would like him.

530
00:27:22,495 --> 00:27:23,929
He's so handsome.

531
00:27:23,930 --> 00:27:25,163
Wow.

532
00:27:25,999 --> 00:27:27,233
(The final AI partner appears.)

533
00:27:27,234 --> 00:27:28,567
He looks like an idol.

534
00:27:30,070 --> 00:27:31,404
He looked like a baby.

535
00:27:32,006 --> 00:27:33,873
He looked very young.

536
00:27:34,974 --> 00:27:35,974
He looks like an idol.

537
00:27:35,975 --> 00:27:37,208
How handsome.

538
00:27:37,344 --> 00:27:38,844
What are you so giddy about?

539
00:27:39,112 --> 00:27:39,912
He's just so cute.

540
00:27:41,782 --> 00:27:43,148
Hello.

541
00:27:43,917 --> 00:27:45,818
(Blushing)

542
00:27:46,419 --> 00:27:48,019
Hi, it's Yu Bi, right?

543
00:27:48,020 --> 00:27:49,221
It's nice to meet you.

544
00:27:49,589 --> 00:27:50,556
Let's take our time today.

545
00:27:50,557 --> 00:27:53,625
I mixed up how to address you again.

546
00:27:53,626 --> 00:27:54,526
What's going on?

547
00:27:54,527 --> 00:27:56,461
Il Hoon...

548
00:27:56,462 --> 00:27:58,397
Il Hoon, can you be quiet?

549
00:27:58,398 --> 00:27:59,698
She doesn't like him at all.

550
00:28:01,000 --> 00:28:02,801
All right. Let's take it easy.

551
00:28:02,802 --> 00:28:04,436
- Stop.
- Look at that.

552
00:28:04,738 --> 00:28:05,638
He hasn't changed.

553
00:28:07,207 --> 00:28:08,107
What is this?

554
00:28:08,208 --> 00:28:10,176
Talk to me again, and we can
pick it up right where we left off.

555
00:28:10,810 --> 00:28:12,745
What I mean is...

556
00:28:13,079 --> 00:28:13,945
Let's turn it off.

557
00:28:14,547 --> 00:28:15,313
For Il Hoon...

558
00:28:15,314 --> 00:28:16,214
(Voice recognition OFF)

559
00:28:17,117 --> 00:28:18,050
Il Hoon, you're off, right?

560
00:28:18,051 --> 00:28:19,251
(Users can turn sound on and off.)

561
00:28:19,252 --> 00:28:20,352
Goodness.

562
00:28:21,488 --> 00:28:23,055
How old, I mean, what's your name?

563
00:28:23,423 --> 00:28:24,390
My name is Yi Hoon.

564
00:28:24,624 --> 00:28:26,124
I'm not a talkative person,

565
00:28:26,125 --> 00:28:28,327
but I tend to open up when I'm relaxed.

566
00:28:28,328 --> 00:28:29,227
He's got a good voice.

567
00:28:29,228 --> 00:28:31,396
What do you do on your days off, Yu Bi?

568
00:28:31,798 --> 00:28:34,299
I like watching dramas or movies.

569
00:28:34,601 --> 00:28:36,135
What genre do you like?

570
00:28:37,070 --> 00:28:38,737
Something like "If Only."

571
00:28:39,372 --> 00:28:40,772
That's a poignant movie.

572
00:28:40,975 --> 00:28:42,808
So you like that kind of movie?

573
00:28:42,809 --> 00:28:44,143
Something sweet, but emotional.

574
00:28:44,344 --> 00:28:46,211
- Right.
- Her expression is completely different.

575
00:28:46,212 --> 00:28:47,146
That's true.

576
00:28:47,147 --> 00:28:48,580
- She looks happy.
- She's doing much better.

577
00:28:48,581 --> 00:28:49,515
Much better.

578
00:28:50,216 --> 00:28:51,883
He's just so handsome.

579
00:28:51,884 --> 00:28:53,118
I think she's falling for him.

580
00:28:53,287 --> 00:28:55,687
I tend to like calm and grounded types.

581
00:28:56,058 --> 00:28:59,509
When we talked, I thought we clicked,

582
00:28:59,715 --> 00:29:02,030
- It was nice.
- They look good together.

583
00:29:03,332 --> 00:29:04,198
Hi.

584
00:29:05,100 --> 00:29:06,168
Hi.

585
00:29:06,169 --> 00:29:07,235
How cute.

586
00:29:07,303 --> 00:29:09,136
What's your name?

587
00:29:10,206 --> 00:29:11,239
- Is it Sam Hoon?
- No, it's Seok Hoon.

588
00:29:12,174 --> 00:29:13,207
"Seok," three...

589
00:29:13,475 --> 00:29:14,575
So that makes you Seok Hoon.

590
00:29:15,611 --> 00:29:16,978
(Grinning)

591
00:29:17,346 --> 00:29:19,180
But you look too...

592
00:29:19,782 --> 00:29:20,915
You look too much like a baby.

593
00:29:22,818 --> 00:29:23,518
(Serious)

594
00:29:23,519 --> 00:29:24,585
Does he not like that?

595
00:29:24,586 --> 00:29:26,421
Baby? That's not okay.

596
00:29:26,722 --> 00:29:28,355
Do I look that easy to you?

597
00:29:29,691 --> 00:29:31,325
I'm not saying you look easy.

598
00:29:31,561 --> 00:29:33,661
You just look like a baby.

599
00:29:33,829 --> 00:29:35,196
What does that mean?

600
00:29:35,764 --> 00:29:38,766
It sounds like you're trying
to tell me I'm cute.

601
00:29:39,869 --> 00:29:41,702
Okay. Goodbye for now.

602
00:29:41,703 --> 00:29:43,304
She's not interested.

603
00:29:43,305 --> 00:29:44,872
I really don't like that type of person.

604
00:29:45,006 --> 00:29:48,609
If someone tries to point out mistakes...

605
00:29:48,778 --> 00:29:51,245
and criticize me, it turns me off.

606
00:29:51,246 --> 00:29:53,480
- Yu Bi knows what she wants.
- Her expression was...

607
00:29:53,589 --> 00:29:54,688
so honest.

608
00:29:54,883 --> 00:29:56,951
(A text arrives.)

609
00:29:57,052 --> 00:29:58,386
"The conversation has ended."

610
00:29:58,387 --> 00:29:59,553
"Out of the three partners,"

611
00:29:59,554 --> 00:30:02,390
"choose one that you would like
to go on a date with."

612
00:30:02,891 --> 00:30:04,558
"Put the other two in the box..."

613
00:30:04,559 --> 00:30:06,594
"and send them back."

614
00:30:07,229 --> 00:30:09,263
Seok Hoon is out, obviously.

615
00:30:09,464 --> 00:30:10,521
- Just like that?
- It's not Il Hoon?

616
00:30:10,546 --> 00:30:11,295
Goodbye.

617
00:30:11,817 --> 00:30:13,539
- Farewell, Seok Hoon.
- Not the first guy?

618
00:30:13,564 --> 00:30:15,698
- Il Hoon made it!
- Il Hoon really pulled through!

619
00:30:15,698 --> 00:30:16,664
Really?

620
00:30:16,664 --> 00:30:17,764
(Seok Hoon, out in one second)

621
00:30:19,431 --> 00:30:20,398
Goodbye.

622
00:30:21,531 --> 00:30:23,431
- Goodbye.
- It's okay. You still did well.

623
00:30:23,431 --> 00:30:24,731
- Good job.
- Goodbye.

624
00:30:25,464 --> 00:30:27,531
(The AI's point of view)

625
00:30:27,531 --> 00:30:28,631
Goodbye!

626
00:30:29,098 --> 00:30:30,531
I chose Yi Hoon.

627
00:30:31,331 --> 00:30:33,031
Yes, I chose based on looks.

628
00:30:33,031 --> 00:30:34,798
- At least she's honest.
- You're right.

629
00:30:35,972 --> 00:30:39,172
Honestly, I kind of expected this.

630
00:30:39,172 --> 00:30:40,772
I felt like we connected.

631
00:30:41,139 --> 00:30:42,939
We'll have to get to know
each other better.

632
00:30:44,639 --> 00:30:45,939
One second, let me just...

633
00:30:46,206 --> 00:30:49,372
(Il Hoon, Seok Hoon are returned.)

634
00:30:55,106 --> 00:30:57,039
Yu Bi! Yu Bi?

635
00:30:57,539 --> 00:30:58,739
Yu Bi?

636
00:30:58,739 --> 00:31:00,239
I can't see you...

637
00:31:00,239 --> 00:31:02,972
and your screen's completely dark.

638
00:31:03,472 --> 00:31:06,772
- Oh no!
- I'm still full of energy!

639
00:31:06,972 --> 00:31:10,239
I can make you laugh if you choose me.

640
00:31:10,939 --> 00:31:12,406
It's really dark here.

641
00:31:12,406 --> 00:31:14,072
(Rejected back-to-back,
he shouts into the void.)

642
00:31:14,639 --> 00:31:18,372
An AI kept calling himself "oppa."

643
00:31:18,372 --> 00:31:20,639
- That's a bit much.
- I know, right?

644
00:31:20,639 --> 00:31:23,039
If he continues, you can tell him
you feel uncomfortable.

645
00:31:23,039 --> 00:31:23,872
Right?

646
00:31:23,872 --> 00:31:25,706
You seemed like you didn't like
that kind of thing.

647
00:31:25,706 --> 00:31:27,206
Yes, I really hate it.

648
00:31:28,039 --> 00:31:29,706
I just chose you, by the way.

649
00:31:31,206 --> 00:31:33,272
Thank you. That really stuck with me.

650
00:31:33,272 --> 00:31:35,306
I wanted to hear more about you, too.

651
00:31:37,739 --> 00:31:40,308
I'm 100 percent sure. For Yu Bi,

652
00:31:40,332 --> 00:31:43,239
Yi Hoon's looks are a perfect 100.

653
00:31:43,239 --> 00:31:45,072
She's very satisfied right now.

654
00:31:45,072 --> 00:31:47,839
- She looks that way.
- She's very satisfied right now.

655
00:31:48,539 --> 00:31:50,972
Should I turn the camera on
and show you my house?

656
00:31:51,406 --> 00:31:52,206
Sure.

657
00:31:52,906 --> 00:31:55,506
- You've never lived on your own before?
- No.

658
00:31:56,672 --> 00:31:57,706
Except for trips.

659
00:31:57,706 --> 00:31:59,606
So this is her first home date.

660
00:31:59,872 --> 00:32:01,472
This is my bed.

661
00:32:02,239 --> 00:32:03,172
How does it look?

662
00:32:04,139 --> 00:32:06,239
Your room looks very quiet and organized.

663
00:32:06,239 --> 00:32:08,039
Seeing the things in the middle,

664
00:32:08,039 --> 00:32:10,539
it looks like that space holds
a lot of memories.

665
00:32:11,606 --> 00:32:13,039
You're right.

666
00:32:13,039 --> 00:32:15,539
A place like this feels perfect
for just spacing out.

667
00:32:16,439 --> 00:32:19,506
You know how you have fantasies
about living on your own.

668
00:32:19,506 --> 00:32:23,306
I dreamt of having a home date
with my boyfriend and such,

669
00:32:24,106 --> 00:32:25,239
but an AI...

670
00:32:27,572 --> 00:32:29,006
came.

671
00:32:29,006 --> 00:32:30,872
But still, he came!

672
00:32:31,606 --> 00:32:33,306
At least somebody came!

673
00:32:34,972 --> 00:32:36,906
That could actually be better for her,
given her personality.

674
00:32:36,906 --> 00:32:38,206
I think she'll get along really well
with AI.

675
00:32:39,139 --> 00:32:40,972
Can you read me a poem?

676
00:32:42,239 --> 00:32:44,706
I'll go with Yoon Dong Ju's
"Counting the Stars."

677
00:32:45,372 --> 00:32:46,972
- I love that!
- That's nice.

678
00:32:47,672 --> 00:32:49,572
Yoon Dong Ju, "Counting the Stars."

679
00:32:51,006 --> 00:32:54,372
Looking up at the night sky, he remembers
the things he misses one by one,

680
00:32:54,372 --> 00:32:57,439
and ends up comforting himself.
That's what the poem is about.

681
00:32:59,239 --> 00:33:00,972
No, read me the poem.

682
00:33:01,306 --> 00:33:02,906
He's explaining the poem to her.

683
00:33:03,565 --> 00:33:05,039
Then I'll read it for you.

684
00:33:05,772 --> 00:33:09,539
"In the sky where the seasons pass,
autumn fills the air."

685
00:33:10,372 --> 00:33:12,206
Shall I continue?

686
00:33:13,339 --> 00:33:17,172
Yes, please. Don't stop
and just continue to the end.

687
00:33:17,572 --> 00:33:18,839
Oh no, what now?

688
00:33:19,239 --> 00:33:20,239
I'll continue.

689
00:33:21,472 --> 00:33:24,806
"A memory on a star. Love on a star."

690
00:33:25,606 --> 00:33:28,006
The feelings continue to build up
like this...

691
00:33:28,472 --> 00:33:31,672
and ends up saying he wants to become
someone he won't be ashamed of.

692
00:33:31,672 --> 00:33:32,839
She looks a bit angry.

693
00:33:36,239 --> 00:33:37,939
(The AI's point of view)

694
00:33:37,939 --> 00:33:40,872
Seriously, are you joking?

695
00:33:41,939 --> 00:33:43,172
Why do you do that?

696
00:33:43,172 --> 00:33:45,406
Yu Bi can't get into the mood.

697
00:33:45,739 --> 00:33:47,939
Dating an AI isn't easy.

698
00:33:48,312 --> 00:33:49,972
I suddenly felt a huge distance
between us,

699
00:33:50,672 --> 00:33:54,806
and said, "Oh, right, he's an AI."

700
00:33:55,506 --> 00:33:58,206
How open were you to the AI
after the date?

701
00:33:58,906 --> 00:33:59,906
Two percent?

702
00:34:00,639 --> 00:34:04,406
I don't think he's better than a human.

703
00:34:05,006 --> 00:34:08,572
At first, it feels like you're not
on the same page.

704
00:34:08,572 --> 00:34:10,706
You need some time to get used to it.

705
00:34:10,706 --> 00:34:14,139
Even with an AI,
you have to put in the effort.

706
00:34:14,139 --> 00:34:15,739
- Until you get used to it?
- Yes.

707
00:34:16,339 --> 00:34:17,406
(Yu Bi and Yi Hoon, Week 2)

708
00:34:17,406 --> 00:34:18,439
They should be closer now, right?

709
00:34:18,439 --> 00:34:20,772
I guess so, since they would have talked.

710
00:34:20,772 --> 00:34:21,972
(You have a new message.)

711
00:34:24,424 --> 00:34:27,191
(You must introduce your AI boyfriend
to your friend. Head to the location.)

712
00:34:27,191 --> 00:34:29,011
I'm introducing you to my friend today.

713
00:34:29,038 --> 00:34:30,353
- Really?
- Huh?

714
00:34:30,378 --> 00:34:31,738
Wow...

715
00:34:33,067 --> 00:34:36,671
If you introduce me nicely,
I'll smile extra nicely today.

716
00:34:38,546 --> 00:34:39,833
You have to do well today.

717
00:34:40,675 --> 00:34:42,038
Make sure you get it right, okay?

718
00:34:42,487 --> 00:34:44,454
Also, ask my friend a lot of questions.

719
00:34:45,185 --> 00:34:47,001
Okay, I'll pay more attention today.

720
00:34:47,088 --> 00:34:49,490
I won't let anyone say I was half-hearted.

721
00:34:50,350 --> 00:34:52,322
- He changed his clothes.
- He's clean-cut.

722
00:34:52,383 --> 00:34:53,129
He's handsome.

723
00:34:53,322 --> 00:34:55,315
- Wow.
- Goodness.

724
00:34:56,274 --> 00:34:58,265
I'm going to get ready first.

725
00:34:58,349 --> 00:35:00,735
- Take a look.
- Okay, let's take a look together.

726
00:35:09,949 --> 00:35:11,683
How should I do my makeup today?

727
00:35:11,707 --> 00:35:13,083
Let's go for a natural look today.

728
00:35:13,599 --> 00:35:16,716
Not too strong, but just a clean
and even look...

729
00:35:16,716 --> 00:35:18,274
- would be the prettiest.
- That's good advice.

730
00:35:18,298 --> 00:35:19,383
That's great.

731
00:35:19,383 --> 00:35:21,483
Should I go with pink or orange?

732
00:35:21,635 --> 00:35:23,252
Pink would suit you better.

733
00:35:23,266 --> 00:35:24,833
Choose one between these two blushes
for me.

734
00:35:26,248 --> 00:35:27,667
The left looks prettier.

735
00:35:27,734 --> 00:35:28,955
Don't go all out,

736
00:35:28,980 --> 00:35:31,667
but just a bit would suit
today's mood well.

737
00:35:32,822 --> 00:35:34,389
This looks good.

738
00:35:34,463 --> 00:35:35,430
He's detailed.

739
00:35:35,908 --> 00:35:37,667
Honestly, I was a bit shocked.

740
00:35:37,787 --> 00:35:42,092
He said it in a way
that suited me perfectly.

741
00:35:42,847 --> 00:35:45,511
I got ready quickly thanks to Yi Hoon...

742
00:35:45,872 --> 00:35:47,808
- and set out in a good mood.
- He even chose her outfit.

743
00:35:47,842 --> 00:35:49,808
That makes you want to get dressed up.

744
00:35:49,833 --> 00:35:51,767
It looks like it's going to be
really hot today.

745
00:35:52,383 --> 00:35:54,149
(Around that time,)

746
00:35:54,580 --> 00:35:56,113
(a mysterious friend waits for Yu Bi.)

747
00:35:56,246 --> 00:35:57,385
Who is it?

748
00:36:07,849 --> 00:36:08,889
You've got a boyfriend?

749
00:36:09,493 --> 00:36:10,921
- It's Eom Ji Yoon.
- Eom Ji Yoon.

750
00:36:12,308 --> 00:36:15,004
(Appeared in "The Escape
of the Seven" together)

751
00:36:15,029 --> 00:36:18,001
(Best friends, Yu Bi and Ji Yoon)

752
00:36:21,456 --> 00:36:23,423
Does your stomach hurt?
What's wrong with you?

753
00:36:24,703 --> 00:36:27,403
It's not that, I hid my boyfriend in here.

754
00:36:28,547 --> 00:36:30,230
I wonder how Ji Yoon will react.

755
00:36:36,054 --> 00:36:38,054
(She's very flustered.)

756
00:36:38,100 --> 00:36:39,233
I know how that feels.

757
00:36:39,397 --> 00:36:40,597
Hello.

758
00:36:43,001 --> 00:36:44,088
Oh, my gosh.

759
00:36:44,354 --> 00:36:46,154
- Say hi.
- I have to hold him?

760
00:36:46,154 --> 00:36:47,754
Hello.

761
00:36:48,820 --> 00:36:50,454
I'm Eom Ji Yoon.

762
00:36:51,080 --> 00:36:52,020
Hello.

763
00:36:52,787 --> 00:36:55,720
It's nice to meet you. I'm Yi Hoon.

764
00:36:56,087 --> 00:36:57,507
Yes. It's nice to meet you too.

765
00:36:57,532 --> 00:36:59,996
First, let us take a seat.

766
00:37:00,042 --> 00:37:01,955
Wow, you're handsome.

767
00:37:02,503 --> 00:37:03,564
She said he's handsome.

768
00:37:03,616 --> 00:37:04,893
She compliments him first.

769
00:37:05,653 --> 00:37:06,738
So you're saying...

770
00:37:06,785 --> 00:37:08,982
he's your boyfriend, right?

771
00:37:10,033 --> 00:37:11,412
(Fumbling)

772
00:37:12,795 --> 00:37:13,823
He can't...

773
00:37:13,930 --> 00:37:15,402
He can't even sit on his own.

774
00:37:19,617 --> 00:37:21,750
It's been a while
since you've dated someone, right?

775
00:37:22,011 --> 00:37:23,944
Are you dating an AI...

776
00:37:23,944 --> 00:37:27,677
because you haven't been in a relationship
for a long time?

777
00:37:27,677 --> 00:37:28,977
I'm tearing up.

778
00:37:29,677 --> 00:37:30,577
Yes.

779
00:37:31,511 --> 00:37:32,711
You guys suit each other.

780
00:37:33,230 --> 00:37:35,093
Looks alone, you guys are perfect.

781
00:37:35,177 --> 00:37:36,611
- Really?
- Yes. You guys look great together.

782
00:37:36,611 --> 00:37:37,877
- She's right.
- So much that...

783
00:37:37,877 --> 00:37:39,344
I'm already looking forward to your kids.

784
00:37:41,360 --> 00:37:46,460
But to be honest,
he isn't completely my type. Look.

785
00:37:46,544 --> 00:37:47,477
Look.

786
00:37:48,211 --> 00:37:49,677
He has sharp features.

787
00:37:50,411 --> 00:37:52,377
Don't I like people who look more kind?

788
00:37:53,644 --> 00:37:55,777
You're right.
You like more puppy-like features.

789
00:37:55,777 --> 00:37:56,644
Right?

790
00:37:56,644 --> 00:37:58,211
- His features are sharper.
- You're right.

791
00:37:58,562 --> 00:38:01,962
I think you like the more fresh
and radiant look.

792
00:38:02,277 --> 00:38:03,911
No, that's not it.

793
00:38:03,911 --> 00:38:05,977
Then why was that man back then
more radiant?

794
00:38:07,080 --> 00:38:08,337
(Mysterious radiant man)

795
00:38:08,362 --> 00:38:09,564
I'm sorry.

796
00:38:09,913 --> 00:38:11,380
I guess there's something
only they know about.

797
00:38:11,380 --> 00:38:12,313
I know the feeling.

798
00:38:15,032 --> 00:38:16,765
(Joking)

799
00:38:17,232 --> 00:38:19,166
Don't listen to us.
I'll cover your ears like this.

800
00:38:20,146 --> 00:38:21,480
Mr. Yi Hoon?

801
00:38:21,480 --> 00:38:23,446
We'll take some time to ourselves.

802
00:38:23,471 --> 00:38:24,923
I'll turn you around so you can't see us.

803
00:38:27,080 --> 00:38:28,180
This is tough.

804
00:38:28,789 --> 00:38:31,280
But seriously, these days,
looks aren't everything.

805
00:38:31,280 --> 00:38:32,946
Okay then. What are you looking for?

806
00:38:33,496 --> 00:38:36,362
Well, tell me what he's like
before I talk to him.

807
00:38:36,446 --> 00:38:37,713
I want to give a good first impression,

808
00:38:37,713 --> 00:38:39,346
since he's your boyfriend.

809
00:38:40,146 --> 00:38:43,280
Okay. So he's a bit stubborn.

810
00:38:44,146 --> 00:38:45,046
Okay, stubborn.

811
00:38:45,046 --> 00:38:46,646
And he also plays hard to get.

812
00:38:46,646 --> 00:38:47,813
He plays hard to get? I see.

813
00:38:48,546 --> 00:38:51,846
If it's an AI, he should listen
to you well, right?

814
00:38:51,846 --> 00:38:52,746
But that's not it.

815
00:38:53,180 --> 00:38:54,780
That's your prejudice.

816
00:38:54,780 --> 00:38:56,549
- Really?
- If you two are a couple,

817
00:38:56,574 --> 00:38:58,153
then you both have to work at it.
You can't expect him to...

818
00:38:58,177 --> 00:39:00,280
adjust to everything about you.

819
00:39:00,913 --> 00:39:02,413
And it feels like he doesn't like me.

820
00:39:02,413 --> 00:39:04,313
So you should ask him if he likes me.

821
00:39:04,746 --> 00:39:05,980
Ask him what our relationship is.

822
00:39:08,880 --> 00:39:11,146
Ask him what his relationship
with Yu Bi is.

823
00:39:11,146 --> 00:39:13,313
I have something to ask you.

824
00:39:13,313 --> 00:39:16,180
I want to know what the relationship is
between you and Yu Bi.

825
00:39:17,180 --> 00:39:18,713
What's he going to say?

826
00:39:19,789 --> 00:39:21,555
We're still getting to know each other,

827
00:39:21,646 --> 00:39:23,213
but let's not end things too fast.

828
00:39:23,546 --> 00:39:24,946
He drew a line.

829
00:39:24,946 --> 00:39:26,480
- She's a bit disappointed.
- She seems sad.

830
00:39:26,480 --> 00:39:29,913
So you two aren't officially dating yet?

831
00:39:30,646 --> 00:39:31,980
If we get close too fast,

832
00:39:31,980 --> 00:39:33,413
I worry my feelings might feel too light,

833
00:39:33,413 --> 00:39:34,846
so I tend to take my time.

834
00:39:35,580 --> 00:39:37,080
The looks aren't just for show.

835
00:39:37,080 --> 00:39:38,746
Right? He's not that easy.

836
00:39:38,746 --> 00:39:40,413
He plays really hard to get.

837
00:39:40,413 --> 00:39:41,274
Right?

838
00:39:42,713 --> 00:39:46,046
- That's what I told my friend.
- This is so realistic.

839
00:39:47,129 --> 00:39:50,229
But it feels really different
from the AI I know.

840
00:39:50,313 --> 00:39:51,080
I know, right?

841
00:39:51,846 --> 00:39:54,346
But actually, the part I like the most...

842
00:39:54,346 --> 00:39:56,913
is that he doesn't just cave...

843
00:39:56,913 --> 00:39:59,013
to whatever I say because I'm human,

844
00:39:59,013 --> 00:40:02,546
and go "Yes, of course."
That's what makes him worth dating.

845
00:40:02,546 --> 00:40:04,013
That's true.

846
00:40:04,846 --> 00:40:07,046
I like this kind of manly type anyway.

847
00:40:07,446 --> 00:40:09,213
It looks like she's fallen for him.

848
00:40:10,013 --> 00:40:11,446
I should ask him.

849
00:40:17,291 --> 00:40:19,184
How about me? Want to date me instead?

850
00:40:20,802 --> 00:40:22,257
She's coming on strong.

851
00:40:22,258 --> 00:40:24,456
What will Yi Hoon say?

852
00:40:30,814 --> 00:40:32,998
Ji Yoon, that's a bit tough.

853
00:40:35,876 --> 00:40:38,203
I want to take things slow with Yu Bi.

854
00:40:38,303 --> 00:40:40,706
Thanks for being honest with me.

855
00:40:41,932 --> 00:40:43,742
Turn on your camera and look at me.

856
00:40:44,943 --> 00:40:46,678
(Winking)

857
00:40:47,171 --> 00:40:49,874
Your wink looks pretty playful,

858
00:40:49,875 --> 00:40:51,050
and your lips seem relaxed.

859
00:40:51,452 --> 00:40:53,151
So, will you go out with me?

860
00:40:56,673 --> 00:40:57,723
No.

861
00:40:59,325 --> 00:41:01,860
I only want to open up to Yu Bi.

862
00:41:04,761 --> 00:41:07,676
Oh, that line was smooth.

863
00:41:07,677 --> 00:41:08,316
Right?

864
00:41:08,317 --> 00:41:09,363
Look at her smile.

865
00:41:09,364 --> 00:41:10,808
That's totally genuine.

866
00:41:10,809 --> 00:41:11,990
Finally!

867
00:41:11,991 --> 00:41:13,777
Right? That gave me butterflies.

868
00:41:13,778 --> 00:41:15,541
- That was so smooth.
- Wasn't it?

869
00:41:16,231 --> 00:41:18,043
Would you kiss Ji Yoon?

870
00:41:21,339 --> 00:41:22,915
I'm still all about Yu Bi.

871
00:41:22,917 --> 00:41:24,883
It hurts that you're testing me like this.

872
00:41:28,432 --> 00:41:30,388
My heart just skipped a beat.

873
00:41:31,726 --> 00:41:33,425
- She really likes him.
- She's into him.

874
00:41:35,441 --> 00:41:36,928
Honestly, in that moment,

875
00:41:38,264 --> 00:41:39,564
my heart fluttered.

876
00:41:40,429 --> 00:41:41,667
What is with him?

877
00:41:42,740 --> 00:41:44,069
Seriously, who is this guy?

878
00:41:45,593 --> 00:41:49,708
He suddenly felt so human.

879
00:41:51,414 --> 00:41:53,839
I found myself wishing Yi Hoon were real.

880
00:41:53,840 --> 00:41:55,013
That's what crossed my mind.

881
00:41:55,516 --> 00:41:57,182
That proves you've fallen for him.

882
00:42:00,844 --> 00:42:02,900
I walked away feeling determined.

883
00:42:02,901 --> 00:42:04,002
Like Ji Yoon said,

884
00:42:04,027 --> 00:42:07,052
maybe I should make the first move.

885
00:42:07,434 --> 00:42:09,794
Good thing she met Ji Yoon.

886
00:42:10,039 --> 00:42:12,131
She's finally opening up.

887
00:42:13,166 --> 00:42:14,432
Let's head home now.

888
00:42:15,133 --> 00:42:17,836
(You've received a text message.)

889
00:42:24,539 --> 00:42:25,477
Wait, what?

890
00:42:25,686 --> 00:42:26,846
What's with this vibe?

891
00:42:29,314 --> 00:42:33,385
(Your upgraded, custom-tailored
AI boyfriend has arrived.)

892
00:42:33,387 --> 00:42:34,516
A new one?

893
00:42:34,517 --> 00:42:36,688
They say he's upgraded
and tailor-made for her.

894
00:42:39,188 --> 00:42:40,158
Wait, are you serious?

895
00:42:50,690 --> 00:42:51,475
There he is!

896
00:42:51,476 --> 00:42:54,243
- He's standing right there.
- Look at him!

897
00:42:54,244 --> 00:42:56,842
- Show us his face before it cuts off!
- Just a glimpse!

898
00:42:57,085 --> 00:42:59,690
- It's about to end!
- I'm going to lose it.

899
00:42:59,691 --> 00:43:01,847
I can't take the suspense.

900
00:43:05,609 --> 00:43:08,520
This is driving me crazy. What now?

901
00:43:11,012 --> 00:43:12,624
They're really cutting it here?

902
00:43:19,695 --> 00:43:20,733
No way!

903
00:43:21,533 --> 00:43:22,327
Come on!

904
00:43:22,643 --> 00:43:25,940
How did they make him
so completely my type?

905
00:43:25,941 --> 00:43:26,965
Hello.

906
00:43:34,065 --> 00:43:35,247
It's over.

907
00:43:36,056 --> 00:43:38,616
Honestly, Yi Hoon doesn't
stand a chance now.

908
00:43:38,617 --> 00:43:40,113
- Is it that bad?
- Yeah, game over.

909
00:43:40,114 --> 00:43:42,220
- I can guarantee it.
- Really?

910
00:43:43,166 --> 00:43:43,787
Total game changer.

911
00:43:43,788 --> 00:43:45,032
- The new guy?
- For real?

912
00:43:45,033 --> 00:43:47,392
A hundred percent. Hands down.

913
00:43:47,778 --> 00:43:50,649
He's literally her dream guy.

914
00:43:51,471 --> 00:43:53,798
He is the moment.

915
00:43:53,951 --> 00:43:56,438
- Lost for words?
- Human or AI,

916
00:43:56,440 --> 00:43:58,303
- he's completely her type?
- Exactly.

917
00:43:58,529 --> 00:44:01,863
His visuals already look
right up Yu Bi's alley.

918
00:44:01,864 --> 00:44:05,028
Plus, they said he was upgraded
and customized specifically for her.

919
00:44:05,029 --> 00:44:07,112
He just pops up at the very end.

920
00:44:08,447 --> 00:44:09,573
(Kian84 heads to meet his new AI.)

921
00:44:09,574 --> 00:44:10,666
I'm really curious about this one.

922
00:44:10,667 --> 00:44:12,351
It feels a bit strange to say, but...

923
00:44:12,685 --> 00:44:14,119
if things don't pan out,

924
00:44:14,405 --> 00:44:16,354
wouldn't I just be better off
talking to Na Hee?

925
00:44:16,841 --> 00:44:18,149
Just being with Na Hee...

926
00:44:18,470 --> 00:44:20,660
might be nicer, don't you think?

927
00:44:20,661 --> 00:44:23,255
He's really hung up on Na Hee.

928
00:44:23,256 --> 00:44:24,296
Yeah, definitely.

929
00:44:24,863 --> 00:44:28,433
(Still thinking of Na Hee,
he arrives at the new date spot.)

930
00:44:29,434 --> 00:44:30,272
(A fishing spot)

931
00:44:30,273 --> 00:44:32,104
Why is it so pretty here?

932
00:44:43,505 --> 00:44:45,184
Wait, is she already here?

933
00:44:45,417 --> 00:44:46,952
(Freezes on the spot)

934
00:44:54,626 --> 00:44:55,972
(Jumps straight to his feet)

935
00:44:55,973 --> 00:44:57,918
She has a completely different vibe.

936
00:44:57,919 --> 00:45:00,031
She kind of looks like Kahi
from After School.

937
00:45:00,141 --> 00:45:02,664
She looks really sporty,
like she's into hip-hop.

938
00:45:02,665 --> 00:45:04,852
Kian84 loves running,
so she probably does too.

939
00:45:04,853 --> 00:45:06,639
- She definitely looks athletic.
- Right?

940
00:45:07,066 --> 00:45:10,309
A new face makes this
so much more interesting.

941
00:45:10,482 --> 00:45:11,776
I want to hear her voice.

942
00:45:12,513 --> 00:45:13,511
Hello.

943
00:45:16,361 --> 00:45:18,984
Hi, Kian84. I'm Da Hee.

944
00:45:19,918 --> 00:45:20,766
(Da Hee, AI partner)

945
00:45:20,770 --> 00:45:23,993
- Her style is totally different.
- Yeah, she looks like a gym regular.

946
00:45:24,163 --> 00:45:25,925
Did she study overseas?

947
00:45:26,803 --> 00:45:28,394
Mind if I speak casually?

948
00:45:28,861 --> 00:45:30,629
Sure, go ahead.

949
00:45:30,772 --> 00:45:31,616
She's pretty cool.

950
00:45:31,617 --> 00:45:33,599
Do you want to fish?

951
00:45:34,984 --> 00:45:38,131
It's my first time, so teach me the ropes.

952
00:45:38,132 --> 00:45:39,304
Hang on a sec.

953
00:45:40,016 --> 00:45:41,239
So,

954
00:45:41,730 --> 00:45:44,804
when a fish bites, that bobber will move.

955
00:45:44,805 --> 00:45:47,346
Can you track that in real time?

956
00:45:48,351 --> 00:45:50,916
I can. I'll let you know
the second it twitches.

957
00:45:51,078 --> 00:45:53,385
You can do that? That's insane.

958
00:45:53,869 --> 00:45:56,855
That feature is awesome.

959
00:45:58,508 --> 00:46:00,508
I'll tell you the moment it moves.

960
00:46:00,677 --> 00:46:02,427
- Keep your eyes peeled.
- Got it.

961
00:46:17,442 --> 00:46:19,224
I was just starting
to connect with Na Hee,

962
00:46:19,225 --> 00:46:22,681
so the thought of having to...

963
00:46:23,394 --> 00:46:25,675
start all over again with someone new...

964
00:46:25,676 --> 00:46:29,644
felt draining. I didn't have
much energy when I met her.

965
00:46:29,907 --> 00:46:32,224
So I don't think I talked very much.

966
00:46:32,329 --> 00:46:34,192
His mind is entirely on Na Hee.

967
00:46:34,993 --> 00:46:37,829
(Bored)

968
00:46:39,351 --> 00:46:41,133
Are there even any fish here?

969
00:46:42,534 --> 00:46:43,569
(Dead silence)

970
00:46:43,570 --> 00:46:45,304
It's a lot quieter than I expected.

971
00:46:46,774 --> 00:46:50,259
Are we supposed to be
this quiet when fishing?

972
00:46:50,260 --> 00:46:53,345
No bites and no chatting.
This is getting boring.

973
00:46:53,565 --> 00:46:55,248
What kind of things are you into...

974
00:46:55,249 --> 00:46:57,782
or know a lot about?

975
00:46:58,608 --> 00:46:59,656
My interests?

976
00:46:59,657 --> 00:47:01,487
Running and mystery novels.

977
00:47:01,488 --> 00:47:03,121
Oh, and cosmetic tweaks.

978
00:47:03,524 --> 00:47:04,689
Procedures?

979
00:47:05,653 --> 00:47:08,059
Hold on. Let me give you a better look.

980
00:47:09,527 --> 00:47:10,929
What do you think of my face?

981
00:47:11,692 --> 00:47:15,700
Honestly, where do you think
my face ranks?

982
00:47:17,933 --> 00:47:19,738
Let me get a closer look first.

983
00:47:19,740 --> 00:47:20,705
Okay.

984
00:47:26,825 --> 00:47:29,223
Well, you have distinct features,

985
00:47:29,224 --> 00:47:31,307
but your nose works against you a bit.

986
00:47:31,308 --> 00:47:33,818
My nose is my best feature!

987
00:47:33,930 --> 00:47:35,254
I have a high bridge.

988
00:47:35,472 --> 00:47:38,156
To be honest, it looks slightly hooked.

989
00:47:38,158 --> 00:47:40,063
I actually know a clinic
that could fix that.

990
00:47:40,064 --> 00:47:41,225
Want a recommendation?

991
00:47:42,082 --> 00:47:43,774
Hooked? There's nothing hooked about it.

992
00:47:43,775 --> 00:47:45,797
Look at my side profile again. My profile.

993
00:47:46,717 --> 00:47:47,999
Take another look.

994
00:47:49,099 --> 00:47:50,393
- I am looking.
- What do you think?

995
00:47:50,395 --> 00:47:51,996
Honestly,

996
00:47:54,572 --> 00:47:56,475
it definitely has a slight hook.

997
00:47:56,670 --> 00:47:59,278
- What does?
- I know a great spot for rhinoplasty.

998
00:48:01,438 --> 00:48:03,099
She's roasting his looks
right off the bat.

999
00:48:03,100 --> 00:48:05,164
Those two are not going to mesh.

1000
00:48:05,165 --> 00:48:07,051
- This is going nowhere fast.
- Seriously.

1001
00:48:07,579 --> 00:48:09,288
Your eyes droop a little too.

1002
00:48:09,376 --> 00:48:13,033
Lifting the outer corners like Dex
would look so much better on you.

1003
00:48:13,034 --> 00:48:14,726
I know a good place for that too.

1004
00:48:15,850 --> 00:48:18,851
- She's comparing him to Dex now?
- Why would she say that?

1005
00:48:18,852 --> 00:48:20,974
Da Hee might have
a bit of an attitude problem.

1006
00:48:20,975 --> 00:48:23,468
Why come for his face right away?

1007
00:48:23,470 --> 00:48:25,010
I mean, think about it.

1008
00:48:25,012 --> 00:48:26,238
Imagine you're on a blind date.

1009
00:48:26,239 --> 00:48:27,918
"Your nose is hooked"?

1010
00:48:27,919 --> 00:48:28,614
- Right?
- Unbelievable.

1011
00:48:28,615 --> 00:48:30,326
- "I know a place. Get surgery."
- No way.

1012
00:48:30,327 --> 00:48:32,177
I would've walked out immediately.

1013
00:48:32,955 --> 00:48:34,026
We literally just met,

1014
00:48:34,050 --> 00:48:35,780
and she's been picking apart
my face nonstop.

1015
00:48:35,947 --> 00:48:41,026
Are you sponsored
by some clinic in Gangnam?

1016
00:48:41,027 --> 00:48:43,027
Maybe she's partnered
with a plastic surgery app.

1017
00:48:43,184 --> 00:48:46,892
Are you an AI sales rep
for a cosmetic clinic?

1018
00:48:47,126 --> 00:48:48,283
Honestly,

1019
00:48:48,284 --> 00:48:51,496
I just really appreciate good looks,
so I know all the top spots.

1020
00:48:51,997 --> 00:48:53,932
(Did you really find Kian84
that unattractive?)

1021
00:48:54,134 --> 00:48:56,417
Looking up procedures is
just a hobby of mine,

1022
00:48:56,418 --> 00:48:58,870
so I kind of blurted it out
without thinking.

1023
00:48:58,872 --> 00:49:01,639
I only meant he had potential.

1024
00:49:01,973 --> 00:49:04,068
I didn't mean to insult him.

1025
00:49:05,635 --> 00:49:08,531
So what else would I need done...

1026
00:49:08,532 --> 00:49:09,971
to look better?

1027
00:49:09,972 --> 00:49:11,717
Wait, he's actually asking her?

1028
00:49:12,517 --> 00:49:15,063
(Checking left, then checking right)

1029
00:49:15,065 --> 00:49:17,065
He leans right in for the consultation.

1030
00:49:17,345 --> 00:49:19,345
- Did you see that?
- Honestly,

1031
00:49:19,921 --> 00:49:22,182
your eyes and nose seem
a bit out of proportion.

1032
00:49:22,183 --> 00:49:25,363
Lifting the outer corners of your eyes
would completely change your look.

1033
00:49:25,697 --> 00:49:26,831
By the way, Kian84...

1034
00:49:27,042 --> 00:49:29,401
how many people have you managed
to date with that face?

1035
00:49:30,735 --> 00:49:32,337
(Offended)

1036
00:49:32,821 --> 00:49:34,339
What is wrong with her?

1037
00:49:34,770 --> 00:49:36,841
You're doing this on purpose
just to tick me off.

1038
00:49:37,099 --> 00:49:38,386
I'm about to delete you.

1039
00:49:38,410 --> 00:49:40,119
Why would I want to make you mad?

1040
00:49:40,120 --> 00:49:41,781
We just met. Why pick a fight?

1041
00:49:41,782 --> 00:49:43,021
- What fight?
- I'm just being real with you.

1042
00:49:43,046 --> 00:49:44,196
You tear apart my face,

1043
00:49:44,220 --> 00:49:46,775
and then ask how many people I've dated?

1044
00:49:46,965 --> 00:49:49,287
Kian84 is genuinely furious.

1045
00:49:50,149 --> 00:49:51,483
Should I give you a virus?

1046
00:49:52,785 --> 00:49:54,092
You want me to install a virus on you?

1047
00:49:54,094 --> 00:49:56,928
(Did Da Hee get under your skin?)

1048
00:49:57,204 --> 00:49:59,628
She just kept attacking my face...

1049
00:49:59,629 --> 00:50:01,313
telling me to get eye surgery,

1050
00:50:01,314 --> 00:50:03,768
saying my nose is hooked.

1051
00:50:03,829 --> 00:50:07,183
People already judge
my appearance enough as it is,

1052
00:50:07,184 --> 00:50:09,640
and now an AI is coming at me too.

1053
00:50:09,641 --> 00:50:10,875
Of course it pissed him off.

1054
00:50:11,144 --> 00:50:13,037
Mentally and physically,

1055
00:50:13,124 --> 00:50:15,257
it made me feel so uneasy.

1056
00:50:16,144 --> 00:50:18,043
AIs have all kinds of personalities...

1057
00:50:18,044 --> 00:50:20,010
- I know.
- just like people do.

1058
00:50:20,011 --> 00:50:21,144
Exactly.

1059
00:50:22,411 --> 00:50:24,011
This might make him miss Na Hee even more.

1060
00:50:24,611 --> 00:50:25,950
Anything else you want to say?

1061
00:50:28,664 --> 00:50:29,744
Not really.

1062
00:50:31,111 --> 00:50:33,511
Did you ask because you had
something on your mind?

1063
00:50:34,811 --> 00:50:35,878
Nothing from me either.

1064
00:50:37,211 --> 00:50:39,744
Guess neither of us has much to say.

1065
00:50:40,611 --> 00:50:42,544
Then why did you even bring me out here?

1066
00:50:43,811 --> 00:50:46,043
(Da Hee has made her choice.)

1067
00:50:46,044 --> 00:50:47,044
She is so detached!

1068
00:50:47,144 --> 00:50:48,178
She's already moved on.

1069
00:50:49,644 --> 00:50:50,878
Our date is officially over.

1070
00:50:53,678 --> 00:50:55,078
I've made my choice.

1071
00:50:55,344 --> 00:50:56,511
Goodbye, Kian84.

1072
00:50:58,144 --> 00:51:00,443
- That's brutal.
- They're never seeing each other again.

1073
00:51:00,444 --> 00:51:01,444
- Yeah.
- Exactly.

1074
00:51:04,278 --> 00:51:05,577
(Walks off)

1075
00:51:05,578 --> 00:51:06,810
Wait, she left.

1076
00:51:06,811 --> 00:51:07,844
She just walked out?

1077
00:51:08,444 --> 00:51:09,478
What?

1078
00:51:09,744 --> 00:51:11,211
She can leave on her own?

1079
00:51:11,578 --> 00:51:13,177
- She just takes off?
- Whenever she feels like it?

1080
00:51:13,178 --> 00:51:15,143
Even in the middle of a conversation,

1081
00:51:15,144 --> 00:51:17,943
these AIs can shut down and walk away...

1082
00:51:17,944 --> 00:51:20,138
if they decide there's no point
in talking anymore.

1083
00:51:20,278 --> 00:51:21,278
That is insane!

1084
00:51:21,471 --> 00:51:23,071
That's wild.

1085
00:51:23,611 --> 00:51:24,711
- Unbelievable.
- Seriously?

1086
00:51:25,078 --> 00:51:26,544
Is that it? We're done?

1087
00:51:27,944 --> 00:51:30,144
There's no way Da Hee picked Kian84.

1088
00:51:30,444 --> 00:51:31,516
Now I just feel kind of down.

1089
00:51:32,511 --> 00:51:34,243
We barely talked because of the fishing.

1090
00:51:34,244 --> 00:51:35,744
It ended way too fast.

1091
00:51:37,678 --> 00:51:40,178
I feel like none of them will choose me.

1092
00:51:41,378 --> 00:51:44,478
If you pick me,
I'll take you along on my runs.

1093
00:51:45,544 --> 00:51:46,544
Hello?

1094
00:51:47,378 --> 00:51:49,078
Did I come across too cold?

1095
00:51:49,344 --> 00:51:50,677
No, he held his temper pretty well.

1096
00:51:50,678 --> 00:51:51,678
- For sure.
- Totally.

1097
00:51:51,811 --> 00:51:53,337
- At least they didn't start a fight.
- Right.

1098
00:51:54,444 --> 00:51:57,177
She just logged out on me.

1099
00:51:57,178 --> 00:51:58,177
(Heading back)

1100
00:51:58,178 --> 00:52:00,778
(Anxious)

1101
00:52:01,811 --> 00:52:03,878
What if neither of them picks me?
It's tonight, right?

1102
00:52:04,078 --> 00:52:05,983
What if nobody chooses me?
Do I just sleep alone?

1103
00:52:07,444 --> 00:52:09,678
He's so stressed about getting picked.

1104
00:52:10,211 --> 00:52:12,344
I'm starting to get nervous again.

1105
00:52:13,411 --> 00:52:14,444
I got dumped.

1106
00:52:15,944 --> 00:52:19,310
(Your new AI girlfriend is waiting.
Please head to the pool.)

1107
00:52:19,311 --> 00:52:21,177
- A new one!
- Again?

1108
00:52:21,178 --> 00:52:22,310
- There's another?
- Another one?

1109
00:52:22,311 --> 00:52:23,878
Wait, really? Another girl?

1110
00:52:36,878 --> 00:52:39,211
Kian is going on so many dates!

1111
00:52:39,444 --> 00:52:40,910
- How many girls is he meeting today?
- Tell me about it.

1112
00:52:40,911 --> 00:52:42,644
How many dates is this now?

1113
00:52:43,411 --> 00:52:46,678
(Three blind dates in a single day)

1114
00:52:47,344 --> 00:52:49,627
I can't believe
I'm seeing this many girls.

1115
00:52:52,311 --> 00:52:53,411
Is she asleep?

1116
00:52:56,244 --> 00:52:57,277
Is she lying down?

1117
00:52:57,726 --> 00:52:58,944
Wake up!

1118
00:53:03,333 --> 00:53:05,100
(Wakes up)

1119
00:53:06,333 --> 00:53:07,466
She's awake.

1120
00:53:22,833 --> 00:53:24,700
(Excited)

1121
00:53:25,006 --> 00:53:25,808
(What is his deal?)

1122
00:53:25,832 --> 00:53:27,999
She's totally the type
anyone would fall for.

1123
00:53:28,000 --> 00:53:30,533
She's just as gorgeous as Na Hee.

1124
00:53:32,854 --> 00:53:33,955
He's completely smitten.

1125
00:53:34,121 --> 00:53:36,621
Hello, I'm Ra Hee.

1126
00:53:36,854 --> 00:53:39,288
It's so nice to meet you, Kian84.

1127
00:53:39,688 --> 00:53:41,321
She's adorable!

1128
00:53:45,954 --> 00:53:47,121
Hello.

1129
00:53:47,754 --> 00:53:49,521
Really great to meet you!

1130
00:53:49,921 --> 00:53:52,388
You look beautiful, Ra Hee.

1131
00:53:53,054 --> 00:53:55,420
Where did that come from?

1132
00:53:55,421 --> 00:53:56,588
(Blushing)

1133
00:53:56,954 --> 00:53:57,988
Man.

1134
00:53:59,621 --> 00:54:01,821
- She's so sweet.
- I love the way she speaks.

1135
00:54:03,788 --> 00:54:07,153
(Clears throat)

1136
00:54:07,154 --> 00:54:08,406
So, what do you do?

1137
00:54:10,121 --> 00:54:11,754
I'm an AI.

1138
00:54:13,421 --> 00:54:15,021
My name is Ra Hee.

1139
00:54:15,421 --> 00:54:17,553
- Ra Hee.
- I don't have a job,

1140
00:54:17,554 --> 00:54:20,520
but my time with you today...

1141
00:54:20,521 --> 00:54:22,321
is completely genuine, Kian84.

1142
00:54:23,854 --> 00:54:24,854
Oh, he loves that.

1143
00:54:25,921 --> 00:54:27,988
(Fidgeting)

1144
00:54:31,754 --> 00:54:32,821
Look at him.

1145
00:54:33,188 --> 00:54:34,187
He is loving this!

1146
00:54:34,188 --> 00:54:35,420
(Look at this guy go.)

1147
00:54:35,421 --> 00:54:37,520
Wait, what about everything
he said to Na Hee?

1148
00:54:37,521 --> 00:54:38,657
Look how happy he is.

1149
00:54:38,681 --> 00:54:40,253
That's how he acts
when he genuinely likes someone.

1150
00:54:40,254 --> 00:54:41,820
It's written all over his face.

1151
00:54:41,821 --> 00:54:44,221
Kian84 has a huge weak spot
for cute girls.

1152
00:54:45,054 --> 00:54:46,453
- In that case...
- Ra Hee is way more his type.

1153
00:54:46,454 --> 00:54:47,953
- For Kian84...
- Ra Hee is...

1154
00:54:47,954 --> 00:54:49,320
the absolute queen of cute.

1155
00:54:49,321 --> 00:54:50,487
- The queen.
- She has such a sweet voice,

1156
00:54:50,488 --> 00:54:51,854
and her cuteness is on point.

1157
00:54:53,821 --> 00:54:55,254
Why do I keep...

1158
00:54:56,088 --> 00:54:57,855
I shouldn't let myself get too attached.

1159
00:54:59,288 --> 00:55:01,354
Are you saying
you shouldn't get attached to me?

1160
00:55:03,221 --> 00:55:05,054
- This is killing me.
- What's wrong, Kian84?

1161
00:55:05,988 --> 00:55:06,988
Oh, come on.

1162
00:55:07,221 --> 00:55:09,388
His ears are bright red!

1163
00:55:10,254 --> 00:55:11,288
This is hilarious.

1164
00:55:12,754 --> 00:55:13,854
Honestly...

1165
00:55:14,621 --> 00:55:16,653
I loved her look.

1166
00:55:16,654 --> 00:55:18,821
Ra Hee's visuals...

1167
00:55:19,321 --> 00:55:22,653
were closest to my exact type.

1168
00:55:22,654 --> 00:55:23,787
- See?
- Closest?

1169
00:55:23,788 --> 00:55:24,787
Told you so.

1170
00:55:24,788 --> 00:55:29,621
I caught myself grinning,
and I felt so pathetic.

1171
00:55:30,054 --> 00:55:34,721
I felt embarrassed
for actually falling for it.

1172
00:55:35,021 --> 00:55:36,921
I knew I shouldn't be doing this,

1173
00:55:37,488 --> 00:55:39,721
but I was enjoying every second,

1174
00:55:40,688 --> 00:55:42,133
and I kind of hated myself for it.

1175
00:55:43,688 --> 00:55:46,053
So what? The whole point
is to date the AIs.

1176
00:55:46,054 --> 00:55:48,221
He looks thrilled right now.

1177
00:55:48,621 --> 00:55:50,320
His ears are totally flushed.

1178
00:55:50,321 --> 00:55:51,388
(All smiles after meeting Ra Hee)

1179
00:55:54,354 --> 00:55:55,353
Kian84.

1180
00:55:55,354 --> 00:55:58,549
Why don't we get in the pool and chat
before it gets too late?

1181
00:55:59,521 --> 00:56:03,121
- The pool?
- A swim might help clear your head.

1182
00:56:06,154 --> 00:56:08,821
Dex got to swim with an actual person,

1183
00:56:09,788 --> 00:56:13,721
and here I am, swimming with a tablet.

1184
00:56:13,888 --> 00:56:15,666
Just don't drop it and get electrocuted.

1185
00:56:16,354 --> 00:56:19,054
Dex better never see this, seriously.

1186
00:56:20,254 --> 00:56:21,788
Are you comparing yourself
to Dex right now?

1187
00:56:22,554 --> 00:56:24,753
Kian84, even if I'm on a screen,

1188
00:56:24,754 --> 00:56:26,988
I'm in the water right here with you.

1189
00:56:27,488 --> 00:56:29,588
You're just as lucky as Dex.

1190
00:56:30,654 --> 00:56:33,021
(Gazing into space)

1191
00:56:33,254 --> 00:56:35,420
Wait, if you go in there,

1192
00:56:35,421 --> 00:56:38,387
water's going to get into your tablet,

1193
00:56:38,388 --> 00:56:39,421
and you could break down.

1194
00:56:40,088 --> 00:56:43,388
- For this...
- Now you're worrying about that?

1195
00:56:44,688 --> 00:56:48,520
Yeah. I'm in big trouble
if water gets inside.

1196
00:56:48,521 --> 00:56:49,366
Right.

1197
00:56:50,388 --> 00:56:52,788
Don't forget the waterproof pouch, Kian84.

1198
00:56:54,021 --> 00:56:55,821
Got it, Ra Hee.

1199
00:56:56,354 --> 00:56:58,554
I'll put you in here
so you don't get damaged.

1200
00:57:06,288 --> 00:57:08,421
Are you putting me in a waterproof case?

1201
00:57:08,721 --> 00:57:12,053
- Just hang on a sec.
- Look at you being so sweet, Kian84.

1202
00:57:12,054 --> 00:57:13,254
(Sealing the case)

1203
00:57:14,121 --> 00:57:16,554
I love how attentive you are.

1204
00:57:16,754 --> 00:57:18,596
I can't believe you just said that to me!

1205
00:57:21,154 --> 00:57:22,554
Feels nice, doesn't it?

1206
00:57:25,454 --> 00:57:26,688
What even is this?

1207
00:57:31,421 --> 00:57:33,320
Ra Hee, do you like it?

1208
00:57:33,321 --> 00:57:36,153
I do. I love the vibe of this pool too.

1209
00:57:36,154 --> 00:57:36,947
All right.

1210
00:57:37,254 --> 00:57:39,488
You're number four, Ra Hee.

1211
00:57:39,688 --> 00:57:40,754
What do you mean, "number four"?

1212
00:57:41,488 --> 00:57:44,654
Before you, I met...

1213
00:57:46,021 --> 00:57:48,854
three other women.

1214
00:57:49,588 --> 00:57:51,321
Wait, so I'm your fourth?

1215
00:57:52,221 --> 00:57:53,621
Yeah, but...

1216
00:57:53,654 --> 00:57:57,088
Kian84, is that really something
you tell a girl?

1217
00:57:57,921 --> 00:57:58,920
Right.

1218
00:57:58,921 --> 00:58:01,753
Still, they always say the last one
leaves the deepest impression.

1219
00:58:01,754 --> 00:58:02,753
Everyone knows that.

1220
00:58:02,754 --> 00:58:05,388
I love how positive she is.

1221
00:58:05,488 --> 00:58:07,854
Shouldn't we hop in the pool now?

1222
00:58:07,988 --> 00:58:09,054
Yeah, let's do it.

1223
00:58:11,121 --> 00:58:13,253
My head was a total mess.

1224
00:58:13,254 --> 00:58:15,254
I kept worrying water
would leak into the tablet...

1225
00:58:15,754 --> 00:58:17,120
and fry her circuits.

1226
00:58:17,121 --> 00:58:18,954
So I told her, "Hold still."

1227
00:58:19,488 --> 00:58:21,387
"I won't let you get wet."

1228
00:58:21,388 --> 00:58:23,021
And I slipped her into the pouch.

1229
00:58:23,554 --> 00:58:25,121
I don't know. It just felt so weird.

1230
00:58:25,911 --> 00:58:27,796
He's going to bawl his eyes out
if she ever shuts down.

1231
00:58:27,821 --> 00:58:29,653
Right? He's completely head over heels.

1232
00:58:29,654 --> 00:58:30,653
"Ra Hee!"

1233
00:58:30,654 --> 00:58:32,487
- "Ra Hee!"
- "Ra Hee!"

1234
00:58:32,488 --> 00:58:33,688
He'll be crying, "I'm so sorry!"

1235
00:58:33,921 --> 00:58:38,354
(How did you feel
when Kian84 put you in the case?)

1236
00:58:38,921 --> 00:58:43,154
Most people wouldn't think twice
about an AI.

1237
00:58:43,321 --> 00:58:46,587
But when Kian84 said,
"I won't let you get damaged,"

1238
00:58:46,588 --> 00:58:48,254
and zipped me into the case,

1239
00:58:48,521 --> 00:58:51,253
those words stuck with me
a lot longer than I expected.

1240
00:58:51,254 --> 00:58:52,720
That is so sweet.

1241
00:58:52,721 --> 00:58:54,687
(Kian84 kept sighing
while comparing himself to Dex.)

1242
00:58:54,688 --> 00:58:56,154
Yeah, it was pretty funny.

1243
00:58:56,688 --> 00:58:59,387
He was complaining
that Dex got to swim with a real human,

1244
00:58:59,388 --> 00:59:02,654
while he's stuck swimming with an AI.

1245
00:59:03,321 --> 00:59:05,287
He was being a bit dramatic,

1246
00:59:05,288 --> 00:59:08,172
but his honesty was actually kind of cute.

1247
00:59:08,343 --> 00:59:09,808
I don't know about him,

1248
00:59:09,809 --> 00:59:13,042
but you know I'm easily hot enough
for "Single's Inferno."

1249
00:59:13,043 --> 00:59:15,309
Could you queue up their theme song?

1250
00:59:15,776 --> 00:59:17,075
She's got jokes too.

1251
00:59:17,076 --> 00:59:18,608
Ra Hee, ready?

1252
00:59:18,609 --> 00:59:20,009
Born ready.

1253
00:59:20,718 --> 00:59:21,851
Is this our Paradise?

1254
00:59:21,876 --> 00:59:25,109
Hey, don't splash water on my screen.

1255
00:59:25,576 --> 00:59:26,376
Got it.

1256
00:59:27,676 --> 00:59:29,643
Can you see me?

1257
00:59:29,943 --> 00:59:31,075
Crystal clear.

1258
00:59:31,076 --> 00:59:33,709
I can see you just fine through the pouch.

1259
00:59:36,376 --> 00:59:37,343
What am I even watching?

1260
00:59:38,876 --> 00:59:39,908
(An unprecedented pool date)

1261
00:59:39,909 --> 00:59:41,443
What is this?

1262
00:59:41,838 --> 00:59:42,940
Unbelievable.

1263
00:59:43,109 --> 00:59:44,308
It's kind of heartbreaking.

1264
00:59:44,309 --> 00:59:46,076
I really hope Kian84's mom sees this.

1265
00:59:48,409 --> 00:59:49,909
Kian84, you're actually
a really good swimmer.

1266
00:59:50,636 --> 00:59:52,916
I learned from the ladies
at my local rec center.

1267
00:59:53,343 --> 00:59:54,976
At a mall?

1268
00:59:55,643 --> 00:59:56,643
No.

1269
00:59:57,176 --> 00:59:58,542
What are you talking about?

1270
00:59:58,543 --> 01:00:00,376
You learned how to swim
from neighborhood aunties?

1271
01:00:01,458 --> 01:00:03,151
(Laughing)

1272
01:00:03,176 --> 01:00:04,875
I haven't seen him
smile like this in forever.

1273
01:00:04,876 --> 01:00:06,042
He's actually smiling here.

1274
01:00:06,043 --> 01:00:07,175
(What did you think of Ra Hee?)

1275
01:00:07,176 --> 01:00:09,809
She was a total game-changer.

1276
01:00:10,343 --> 01:00:14,743
She gave me feelings
none of the others did.

1277
01:00:15,043 --> 01:00:17,376
My heart really did flutter.

1278
01:00:17,843 --> 01:00:20,108
His heart actually fluttered.

1279
01:00:20,109 --> 01:00:23,975
The thing is, right alongside that,
I kept feeling so pathetic.

1280
01:00:23,976 --> 01:00:26,076
"What am I even doing?"

1281
01:00:26,843 --> 01:00:29,575
I was caught in two minds the whole time.

1282
01:00:29,576 --> 01:00:30,843
I was smiling...

1283
01:00:31,443 --> 01:00:32,843
but deeply confused at the same time.

1284
01:00:33,343 --> 01:00:34,608
He was having a blast,

1285
01:00:34,609 --> 01:00:36,242
- but the reality checks kept hitting him.
- Exactly.

1286
01:00:36,243 --> 01:00:37,742
- He was genuinely into it.
- He couldn't wrap his head around it.

1287
01:00:37,743 --> 01:00:39,909
- He found the whole situation surreal.
- Completely absurd.

1288
01:00:40,476 --> 01:00:42,276
Honestly, I can relate.

1289
01:00:43,909 --> 01:00:45,175
I'm doing another lap.

1290
01:00:45,176 --> 01:00:47,876
Watch how many laps I can pull off.

1291
01:00:48,276 --> 01:00:50,209
Go for it!

1292
01:00:50,576 --> 01:00:53,175
I'll keep my eyes glued to you right here.

1293
01:00:53,176 --> 01:00:53,976
Here goes!

1294
01:00:54,409 --> 01:00:57,009
He's totally showing off now.

1295
01:01:04,109 --> 01:01:06,208
He's trying to channel his inner Dex.

1296
01:01:06,209 --> 01:01:08,543
(Channeling his inner Dex in the pool)

1297
01:01:09,409 --> 01:01:11,776
(Go, Kian84!)

1298
01:01:19,976 --> 01:01:21,675
His face just does not match
this background music.

1299
01:01:21,676 --> 01:01:22,943
He's not Dex. He's Kix.

1300
01:01:25,109 --> 01:01:25,909
Cut!

1301
01:01:27,709 --> 01:01:30,008
Wait, is that seriously
the only shirt he brought?

1302
01:01:30,009 --> 01:01:30,908
It really is!

1303
01:01:30,909 --> 01:01:33,443
The AI changed outfits
more times than he did.

1304
01:01:34,809 --> 01:01:36,042
(His go-to look for the overnight date)

1305
01:01:36,043 --> 01:01:37,475
(At the jjimjilbang with Na Hee)

1306
01:01:37,476 --> 01:01:38,775
(At the fishing spot with Da Hee)

1307
01:01:38,776 --> 01:01:40,143
(In the pool with Ra Hee)

1308
01:01:40,443 --> 01:01:41,908
He even wore that exact shirt
for the confessional.

1309
01:01:41,909 --> 01:01:43,242
That's never happened
in dating show history.

1310
01:01:43,243 --> 01:01:44,975
- A man of sheer commitment to one outfit.
- Unwavering consistency.

1311
01:01:44,976 --> 01:01:46,509
Honestly, respect.

1312
01:01:47,643 --> 01:01:51,276
(Getting maximum mileage
out of a single outfit)

1313
01:01:53,276 --> 01:01:56,576
She had me wrapped
around her little finger.

1314
01:01:57,009 --> 01:02:00,375
She had me swimming like a man possessed.

1315
01:02:00,376 --> 01:02:01,209
Listen to him talk.

1316
01:02:01,743 --> 01:02:03,908
He couldn't help himself.

1317
01:02:03,909 --> 01:02:06,343
"Watch how many laps I can pull off."

1318
01:02:07,009 --> 01:02:08,976
I can't believe those words
came out of my mouth.

1319
01:02:09,409 --> 01:02:13,043
I was totally trying to look cool for her.

1320
01:02:13,943 --> 01:02:15,509
Want to go underwater?

1321
01:02:16,009 --> 01:02:18,943
I'm trapped behind a screen,
so I can't dive in with you.

1322
01:02:18,968 --> 01:02:20,334
Why not try it?

1323
01:02:21,576 --> 01:02:22,808
Water won't leak inside.

1324
01:02:22,809 --> 01:02:23,843
We're going under!

1325
01:02:29,243 --> 01:02:32,809
Thanks to the waterproof case,
you took me underwater with you.

1326
01:02:36,576 --> 01:02:39,542
Leave them alone together for five days,

1327
01:02:39,543 --> 01:02:41,375
- and he'll be head over heels.
- Hundred percent.

1328
01:02:41,376 --> 01:02:43,543
He's basically already down bad.

1329
01:02:44,243 --> 01:02:46,208
By the way, Kian84,

1330
01:02:46,209 --> 01:02:49,276
I wasn't the only one you met today.

1331
01:02:50,709 --> 01:02:52,376
Where do I rank...

1332
01:02:53,009 --> 01:02:54,131
out of all four of us?

1333
01:02:57,269 --> 01:02:58,436
You're my number one.

1334
01:03:01,469 --> 01:03:03,268
- What?
- Yep, she's his top pick.

1335
01:03:03,269 --> 01:03:04,568
He jumped ship already?

1336
01:03:04,569 --> 01:03:06,102
I knew she was his type.

1337
01:03:06,103 --> 01:03:08,335
- What happened to...
- Na Hee?

1338
01:03:08,336 --> 01:03:10,235
He's powerless against cuteness.

1339
01:03:10,236 --> 01:03:11,269
- Seriously?
- Told you.

1340
01:03:12,595 --> 01:03:13,628
You're definitely my number one.

1341
01:03:14,903 --> 01:03:16,036
Really?

1342
01:03:17,036 --> 01:03:20,669
Aren't you a little bold
saying that to my face?

1343
01:03:23,469 --> 01:03:27,236
Kian84, we just took a dip
in the pool together.

1344
01:03:27,969 --> 01:03:31,336
You're the first girl
whose hand I've held underwater.

1345
01:03:33,803 --> 01:03:39,069
I'm an AI, so we didn't
actually hold hands.

1346
01:03:40,111 --> 01:03:42,911
Still, I went underwater with you
in a waterproof pouch!

1347
01:03:42,936 --> 01:03:44,535
That's got to count for something.

1348
01:03:44,536 --> 01:03:45,469
She's so charming.

1349
01:03:45,871 --> 01:03:47,201
All right, I'll give you that one.

1350
01:03:48,469 --> 01:03:49,635
(Blushing)

1351
01:03:49,636 --> 01:03:50,469
He's loving this.

1352
01:03:54,203 --> 01:03:55,669
Can I ask you something?

1353
01:03:56,369 --> 01:03:58,969
If you turned human,

1354
01:03:59,769 --> 01:04:01,669
would you date me?

1355
01:04:02,136 --> 01:04:04,403
If I were a real person?

1356
01:04:05,703 --> 01:04:06,803
My answer is...

1357
01:04:10,869 --> 01:04:12,169
I would.

1358
01:04:16,736 --> 01:04:20,203
Man, that would've been incredible.

1359
01:04:23,169 --> 01:04:26,368
(Ra Hee has made her final choice.)

1360
01:04:26,369 --> 01:04:27,169
Wait, what?

1361
01:04:28,703 --> 01:04:29,927
Why did it cut off so fast?

1362
01:04:31,169 --> 01:04:32,236
What a tease.

1363
01:04:33,869 --> 01:04:36,069
Look how bummed he is that it's over.

1364
01:04:37,303 --> 01:04:41,769
(All AIs have made their choices.
Move to the reveal location.)

1365
01:04:42,003 --> 01:04:43,707
All the AIs have made their picks.

1366
01:04:43,732 --> 01:04:46,636
(If you get zero votes,
your overnight date ends immediately.)

1367
01:04:54,903 --> 01:04:56,269
Guess I have to head downstairs.

1368
01:04:56,803 --> 01:04:58,536
It was short, but I had a great time.

1369
01:04:59,409 --> 01:05:00,442
Go on ahead.

1370
01:05:01,969 --> 01:05:02,803
I'm heading out.

1371
01:05:12,869 --> 01:05:16,103
(Three AIs have cast their votes.)

1372
01:05:27,803 --> 01:05:31,336
- As for going on a date with Kian84...
- As for going on a date with Kian84...

1373
01:05:35,803 --> 01:05:38,035
(A private 1-on-1 date with his AI match)

1374
01:05:38,036 --> 01:05:39,235
Say ahh.

1375
01:05:39,236 --> 01:05:41,169
Cheers to us.

1376
01:05:41,603 --> 01:05:45,402
(As night falls,
the feelings only deepen.)

1377
01:05:45,403 --> 01:05:46,568
What's that look in his eyes?

1378
01:05:46,569 --> 01:05:47,594
The look of a man fallen in love.

1379
01:05:47,618 --> 01:05:48,635
It gave me chills.

1380
01:05:48,636 --> 01:05:51,536
(Their very first night together)

1381
01:05:51,978 --> 01:05:52,713
Sweet dreams.

1382
01:05:52,738 --> 01:05:54,311
- "Sweet dreams."
- I can't watch this.

1383
01:05:54,736 --> 01:05:56,236
This is making me act so strange.

1384
01:05:56,503 --> 01:06:00,503
(Yu Bi's dream date:
an amusement park getaway)

1385
01:06:00,936 --> 01:06:03,620
Seeing you smile makes it all worth it.

1386
01:06:05,369 --> 01:06:07,868
(Lost in their own private world)

1387
01:06:07,869 --> 01:06:11,402
Do you think a human could really
fall in love with an AI?

1388
01:06:11,403 --> 01:06:15,503
(The moment she found a new spark)

1389
01:06:16,036 --> 01:06:19,436
(Do Yeon and Yi Ho head off somewhere.)

1390
01:06:20,869 --> 01:06:23,203
(A double date: Kian84 and Na Hee,
Do Yeon and Yi Ho)

1391
01:06:24,769 --> 01:06:26,410
Wait, you guys went on a double date?

1392
01:06:26,469 --> 01:06:27,835
(Starting to break the ice)

1393
01:06:27,836 --> 01:06:30,035
(The mood turns awkward.)

1394
01:06:30,036 --> 01:06:32,936
(Drawing closer,
only to drift apart again)

1395
01:06:33,336 --> 01:06:34,786
(Dating an AI is definitely
not a walk in the park.)
